{"parentUuid":"8408a7c5-42f0-41d2-90ca-1be694c5d50f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_016dMLpENffKthAdCKaYyg5a","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"if [ -n \"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR:-}\" ] && [ -x /bin/zsh ]; then exec /bin/zsh -fc 'LC_ALL=C␤export CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-$PPID}␤export CMUX_AGENT_HOOK_INVOKER_PID=$PPID␤cmux_fallback() { { print -rn -- \"$cmux_p\"; /bin/cat; } | /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3; exit $?; }␤zmodload zsh/system zsh/datetime zsh/files 2>/dev/null || exec /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3␤cmux_p= cmux_c= cmux_e=0␤while (( ${#cmux_p} < 262144 )); do sysread -i 0 -s 65536 cmux_c || { cmux_e=$?; break; }; cmux_p+=$cmux_c; done␤[[ -n ${CMUX_SURFACE_ID:-} && ${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED:-} != 1 ]] || { (( cmux_e == 5 )) || /bin/cat >/dev/null; print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3; exit 0; }␤cmux_d=$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR␤(( cmux_e == 5 )) && [[ -f $cmux_d/keys ]] || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤cmux_r=\"cmux-agent-hook-v1\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"claude\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"$2\"$'\\''\\n'\\''␤for cmux_k in ${(f)\"$(<$cmux_d/keys)\"}; do (( ${+parameters[$cmux_k]} )) && cmux_r+=\"$cmux_k=${(P)cmux_k}\"$'\\''\\0'\\''; done␤cmux_r+=$'\\''\\0'\\''\"$cmux_p\"␤(( ${#cmux_r} <= 524288 )) || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤umask 077␤cmux_n=$cmux_d/$epochtime[1].$epochtime[2]-$$␤{ print -rn -- \"$cmux_r\" >| $cmux_n.tmp && mv -f -- $cmux_n.tmp $cmux_n.rec; } 2>/dev/null || { rm -f -- $cmux_n.tmp 2>/dev/null; cmux_fallback \"$1\"; }␤if zsystem flock -t 0 -r -f cmux_l $cmux_d/forwarder.lock 2>/dev/null; then␤  zsystem flock -u $cmux_l␤  rm -- $cmux_n.rec 2>/dev/null && cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤fi␤print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3' cmux-hook 'cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; fi' pre-tool-use 3>&1 1>&2; else cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; fi; fi","durationMs":57},"type":"attachment","uuid":"548db8d8-0c66-43b5-858c-a3bbbba7e8f7","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:06:47.227Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"8408a7c5-42f0-41d2-90ca-1be694c5d50f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"43c3a7a1-d74f-4cf0-a7b9-2b1df3091632","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016dMLpENffKthAdCKaYyg5a","type":"tool_result","content":"10:`DECISIONS.md D<n>`. The plans that built Bastion, phase by phase, are in\n35:| D1 | Rust for all Bastion code. Another language only where no Rust path exists, named in §4 with its reason. |\n70:  verdict (F4)?\n      77 DECISIONS.md","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0edf2a8b-9af6-43b8-9bdf-9a6efc8ac57f","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:06:47.489Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"10:`DECISIONS.md D<n>`. The plans that built Bastion, phase by phase, are in\n35:| D1 | Rust for all Bastion code. Another language only where no Rust path exists, named in §4 with its reason. |\n70:  verdict (F4)?\n      77 DECISIONS.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":77,"lines":["+# Bastion decisions","+","+Bastion is a software factory you can govern. A request goes in, agents work","+it through a workflow of steps a person can watch and gate, and a reviewed","+change comes out. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server`","+runs the factory on the iii engine, and clients such as the iced desktop app","+reach it over HTTP.","+","+This file holds the goals and the decisions the code cites as","+`DECISIONS.md D<n>`. The plans that built Bastion, phase by phase, are in","+git history.","+","+## Goals and non-goals","+","+**Goals:**","+","+1. A person sees what every job does and decides what it may do.","+2. A change Bastion lands passed the checks the owner asked for, with the","+   evidence on the job.","+3. A restart, an outage or a lost VM never loses a record or corrupts a job.","+4. Any client and any number of servers, through one API.","+","+**Non-goals for now:** a web client, managed hosting, a plugin system for","+code-defined guards (rules stay data, per D20 and D26), and a sign-in with a","+Claude subscription (D36). Multi-user servers and hosting stay open","+questions (below), not non-goals.","+","+## Decisions","+","+Each decision keeps the number the code cites. Numbers not listed were","+retired with the old plan.","+","+| # | Decision |","+|---|---|","+| D1 | Rust for all Bastion code. Another language only where no Rust path exists, named in §4 with its reason. |","+| D4 | One dark theme, purple as the main color. Its tokens live in `crates/bastion-desktop/src/theme.rs`. |","+| D6 | Every Bastion worker is a Rust binary on `iii-sdk` 0.25.0, started by compose through `scripts.run`. |","+| D7 | A stock iii worker comes first. Bastion writes a worker only for what no pinned worker does. |","+| D8 | Records live in the `database` worker as typed columns. Each row carries a `rev`, and a stale write is refused. |","+| D10 | Updates are pushed, never polled: the server observes the engine, and clients follow the server's events (D29). |","+| D13 | The local server starts the stack (`iii compose`) and attaches to one that already runs. The stack goes down when the server stops. A client attaches to the local server or starts it, and quitting a client leaves both running. |","+| D14 | Every agent turn runs in an `iii-sandbox` VM on its job's worktree. No credential enters the VM; pushes and pull requests happen on the host. |","+| D16 | A note on a step goes to the agent word for word as its next brief. A fix loop stops after a set count, or sooner when a refusal repeats word for word. |","+| D17 | Every job runs a workflow. A free-form task is a short workflow, not a second mode. |","+| D18 | The factory's rules live in `bastion-core`: pure functions from an event and a state to a new state and effects, with no I/O and no `async`. |","+| D19 | The seams are Cargo dependencies, and `scripts/check-seams.sh` fails CI when one is crossed. Only the engine adapter imports `iii-sdk`. Clients depend on `bastion-protocol` and the client library only. |","+| D20 | Every constraint and capability is enforced in a hook, and its rung is data, so an eval can name what changed. |","+| D21 | The audit record is a hash chain with one writer. Each entry carries an HMAC-SHA256 of its fields and the entry before it, keyed with a secret outside the record. |","+| D22 | An eval compares two harness configurations on the same requests from the same commit, and reports the difference with the decisions behind it. |","+| D23 | Forge, tracker, CI, model providers and notifications are adapters behind seams, chosen in Settings. |","+| D25 | Every rule belongs to one layer: the charter (the repository's own), the harness (an agent's calls), or the factory (the workflow). |","+| D26 | Rules, grants and settings are data in the server's database, versioned, edited on the pages; first-run defaults come from `seed/governance.sql`. |","+| D27 | The server is the source of truth and holds all business logic. A client shows state and sends a person's actions, nothing more. |","+| D28 | The API is HTTP with JSON, one route per action on one resource, typed in `bastion-protocol`, with a bearer token on every request. |","+| D29 | Push is server-sent events on `GET /events`, with ids. A client that reconnects with `Last-Event-ID` gets what it missed, or a `resync`. |","+| D30 | A client keeps a list of servers, each a name, a URL and a token in the OS keychain. `local` is the server on this machine. A job runs on one server. |","+| D31 | A server has people with roles: an admin manages it, a member submits and acts on their own jobs, a viewer reads. Tokens are issued, shown once and kept as a hash. Every record names its actor. |","+| D32 | A server listens on loopback unless it has a TLS certificate and key. |","+| D33 | Each step is lights-on or dark. A workflow's level follows from its steps. No step waits on a timer. Every decision is logged, whatever the dial. |","+| D34 | Model provider keys live in the stack's vault, read only by `llm-router`, never in the environment and never returned. |","+| D35 | A workflow is a graph of steps a person edits on a canvas. Steps pass declared results to the steps linked after them. |","+| D36 | Claude takes an API key only. No Claude subscription sign-in. |","+| D37 | The desktop client is a native Rust app on `iced`. It holds no factory logic and reaches a server only through the client library. |","+| D38 | Every client goes through `crates/bastion-client`: the server list, typed calls, and the event stream. A new interface adds pages, not a second way to talk to a server. |","+","+## Open questions","+","+- **Dark to merge.** ghola never lets a factory merge unattended; Bastion's","+  dark dial can run to merge. Should merge always need a person, or a machine","+  verdict (F4)?","+- **Configuration in git.** ghola keeps configuration in files under review;","+  Bastion keeps it in the database with versions (D26). Should rules also be","+  importable as files, such as team rule packs shared by servers?","+- **Multi-user hosting.** A shared server with people and TLS works today.","+  Is hosted Bastion a goal?","+- **Unused stack workers.** C4 lists them; some may be the harness's","+  dependencies."]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e6874977-c69e-4904-ba1d-927863054bf3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8408a7c5-42f0-41d