{"parentUuid":"23fe8b22-0a82-4df4-854d-431256f1cb5e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"43c3a7a1-d74f-4cf0-a7b9-2b1df3091632","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wq4MFm2G52n4WgLmUr3DYy","type":"tool_result","content":"## 4. The repository\n\n```\ncrates/\n  bastion-core/        the factory's rules (D18)\n  bastion-protocol/    the API's types and routes (D28)\n  bastion-server/      the server: HTTP, events, factory adapter, store,\n                       gate, audit, stack; src/engine/ is the iii seam\n  bastion-client/      the client library (D38), from phase I\n  bastion-desktop/     the iced client (D37)\nworkers/\n  bastion-openai-compat/   OpenAI-compatible hosts as router providers\nseed/                  first-run rules, grants and workflows (D26)\nworker-compose.yaml    the stack the local server starts\ndocs/engine-findings.md   what the engine was found to do, and on which versions\n```\n\nCode in another language (D1): `.pi/extensions/entire/index.ts`, generated\nby the Entire tool, not Bastion code.\n\n## 5. Phases\n## Open questions\n\n- **Dark to merge.** ghola never lets a factory merge unattended; Bastion's\n  dark dial can run to merge. Should merge always need a person, or a machine\n  verdict (F4)?\n- **Configuration in git.** ghola keeps configuration in files under review;\n  Bastion keeps it in the database with versions (D26). Should rules also be","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0a1b7c1b-9a3e-421e-9cf8-82ede314d535","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:06:50.258Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## 4. The repository\n\n```\ncrates/\n  bastion-core/        the factory's rules (D18)\n  bastion-protocol/    the API's types and routes (D28)\n  bastion-server/      the server: HTTP, events, factory adapter, store,\n                       gate, audit, stack; src/engine/ is the iii seam\n  bastion-client/      the client library (D38), from phase I\n  bastion-desktop/     the iced client (D37)\nworkers/\n  bastion-openai-compat/   OpenAI-compatible hosts as router providers\nseed/                  first-run rules, grants and workflows (D26)\nworker-compose.yaml    the stack the local server starts\ndocs/engine-findings.md   what the engine was found to do, and on which versions\n```\n\nCode in another language (D1): `.pi/extensions/entire/index.ts`, generated\nby the Entire tool, not Bastion code.\n\n## 5. Phases\n## Open questions\n\n- **Dark to merge.** ghola never lets a factory merge unattended; Bastion's\n  dark dial can run to merge. Should merge always need a person, or a machine\n  verdict (F4)?\n- **Configuration in git.** ghola keeps configuration in files under review;\n  Bastion keeps it in the database with versions (D26). Should rules also be","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"1ac8d77d-7276-4ada-9fff-8cb482ef176a","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"23fe8b22-0a82-4df4-854d-431256f1cb5e","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
