{"parentUuid":"bc519780-2586-41eb-84f0-d7df1c84e81a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwWXCCTZ3FAYizeNgqPn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I checked PLAN.md: every phase was done. So I deleted it and moved what the code still needs into DECISIONS.md (commit `93f41fd`). That commit is local; I have not pushed it, because you didn't ask for a push this time.\n\n**PLAN.md replaced by DECISIONS.md**\n- DECISIONS.md holds the goals and non-goals, the 30 decisions, and the four open questions, as you chose.\n- 48 files cited `PLAN.md D<n>`. Each citation now reads `DECISIONS.md D<n>`, and all 19 cited numbers exist in the new file. CLAUDE.md and the README point to it.\n- I removed the citations of phases, such as `F10` and `I4`. The phases and their progress notes are in git history.\n- D1 used to point at the repository section, which is gone. Its one exception (`.pi/extensions/entire/index.ts`) is now written into D1.\n- The comment in `worker-compose.yaml` was out of date: it said the verify was still to come. It now says the packaged worker is unused, because the verify runs in a VM of its own.\n- My memory notes now point at DECISIONS.md.\n\n**v0.1.1 is released**\n- All three builds passed, and the signature checks against `scripts/minisign.pub`.\n- The Homebrew tap has the new formula and cask (`fad3190`), and the site says 0.1.1 (`6b9cb2e`).\n\nTo get the fixes in the app you installed:\n\n```\n! brew upgrade bastion\n```\n\n**CI change on the way:** Ubuntu 26.04 runners failed the apt step twice. So CI now runs its Linux check on `ubuntu-24.04`, the image the release builds use. The apt step also retries each fetch 3 times and stops after 15 minutes.\n\nI'm ready for the first page."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":425,"cache_read_input_tokens":228097,"output_tokens":602,"output_