{"parentUuid":"563f82e8-1f2f-4ebc-84ca-0f88487e72ff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZCxzoqBsAD2MGCejpV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The tray is removed from the code (`b536884`), and fmt, the seam check, clippy and the tests all pass. The safeguard passed too.\n\n- **Removed:** the `bastion-tray` crate, its icon, and the code in the desktop that started it. Packaging, `install.sh` and the seam check no longer list it.\n- **CI:** the Linux apt step (GTK, app indicator) is gone from CI and from the release. It came in with the tray, and CI ran Linux without it before. That also removes the step that kept failing on Ubuntu mirrors.\n- **Notifications:** the tray showed the system notifications for jobs that wait, fail or land. Those are now gone. The window still shows the waiting count in its title and on Jobs, and the chat webhook still posts notices. If you want system notifications back, the window could show them again; say so and I'll add it.\n- **Site:** I deleted the \"Watch it with the window closed\" section and its nav link, and synced `install.sh` (`313e0a1`, in the gh-pages repo). Voice-check finds nothing new.\n\nNothing is pushed: two commits on `main` (`93f41fd`, `b536884`) and the site commit. v0.1.1 still ships the tray, so if the site goes out now it will not match the release. The usual next step is to push everything and release v0.1.2. Say the word and I'll do both.\n\nThe old installed tray is still running (PID 91843). To stop it, run `! kill 91843`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":377,"cache_read_input_tokens":241424,"output_tokens":480,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":377,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"