{"parentUuid":"38ce2c27-3654-4b44-afc7-30d85c6a7a43","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"02b5e827-a917-46e4-a3d9-305981eb3231","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MKQVwWiaNn6ADePnA8qrcg","type":"tool_result","content":"# Bastion\n\nBastion is a software factory you can govern. A request goes in, agents work\nit through a workflow, and a reviewed change comes out. A workflow is a graph\nof steps (Bastion's own stages, skills, prompts and commands) that you see on\na canvas, and each step waits for your approval or runs on its own, as you set\nit. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server` runs the factory on\nthe [iii](https://iii.dev) engine, and the desktop app (on\n[iced](https://iced.rs)) and the `bastion` command line talk to it over HTTP.\nIt's early, and [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) holds the goals and the decisions\nbehind it.\n\n## Install\n\nOn an Apple Silicon Mac or on Linux, install the server and the CLI, and add\n`--desktop` for the app:\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://tacoda.github.io/bastion/install.sh | sh -s -- --desktop\n```\n\nOn a Mac, Homebrew works too: `brew install --cask tacoda/bastion/bastion`.\nThe installer checks each download against the release's signed checksums,\nand `bastion update` moves you to the newest release. On a Linux VM, add\n`--service` to run the server as a systemd user service.\n\n## Run it from source\n\n```sh\ncargo build -p bastion-server\ncargo run -p bastion-desktop\n```\n\nREADME [argument]  (587 words, 1 findings)\n  - first person low for argument register: 0.0/1k words (min 2.0); no author present is why a page reads cold\n\nrecycled across corpus (5-grams in 7+ pages):\n\n1 findings across 1 page(s)\nchain: voicecheck -> /humanizer (tone) -> /slopbeth (slop) -> voicecheck (gate)\nno later stage may reintroduce a finding above","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"51f0c518-3b4d-4a0f-98d8-80f748d42339","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:51:18.481Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Bastion\n\nBastion is a software factory you can govern. A request goes in, agents work\nit through a workflow, and a reviewed change comes out. A workflow is a graph\nof steps (Bastion's own stages, skills, prompts and commands) that you see on\na canvas, and each step waits for your approval or runs on its own, as you set\nit. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server` runs the factory on\nthe [iii](https://iii.dev) engine, and the desktop app (on\n[iced](https://iced.rs)) and the `bastion` command line talk to it over HTTP.\nIt's early, and [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) holds the goals and the decisions\nbehind it.\n\n## Install\n\nOn an Apple Silicon Mac or on Linux, install the server and the CLI, and add\n`--desktop` for the app:\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://tacoda.github.io/bastion/install.sh | sh -s -- --desktop\n```\n\nOn a Mac, Homebrew works too: `brew install --cask tacoda/bastion/bastion`.\nThe installer checks each download against the release's signed checksums,\nand `bastion update` moves you to the newest release. On a Linux VM, add\n`--service` to run the server as a systemd user service.\n\n## Run it from source\n\n```sh\ncargo build -p bastion-server\ncargo run -p bastion-desktop\n```\n\nREADME [argument]  (587 words, 1 findings)\n  - first person low for argument register: 0.0/1k words (min 2.0); no author present is why a page reads cold\n\nrecycled across corpus (5-grams in 7+ pages):\n\n1 findings across 1 page(s)\nchain: voicecheck -> /humanizer (tone) -> /slopbeth (slop) -> voicecheck (gate)\nno later stage may reintroduce a finding above","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":9,"newStart":5,"newLines":26,"lines":[" of steps (Bastion's own stages, skills, prompts and commands) that you see on"," a canvas, and each step waits for your approval or runs on its own, as you set"," it. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server` runs the factory on","-the [iii](https://iii.dev) engine, and the desktop client (Rust, on","-[iced](https://iced.rs)) talks to it over HTTP. It's early, and","-[DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) holds the goals and the decisions behind it.","+the [iii](https://iii.dev) engine, and the desktop app (on","+[iced](https://iced.rs)) and the `bastion` command line talk to it over HTTP.","+It's early, and [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) holds the goals and the decisions","+behind it.","+","+## Install","+","+On an Apple Silicon Mac or on Linux, install the server and the CLI, and add","+`--desktop` for the app:","+","+```sh","+curl -fsSL https://tacoda.github.io/bastion/install.sh | sh -s -- --desktop","+```","+","+On a Mac, Homebrew works too: `brew install --cask tacoda/bastion/bastion`.","+The installer checks each download against the release's signed checksums,","+and `bastion update` moves you to the newest release. On a Linux VM, add","+`--service` to run the server as a systemd user service.","+","+## Run it from source"," "," ```sh"," cargo build -p bastion-server"]},{"oldStart":46,"oldLines":7,"newStart":63,"newLines":9,"lines":[" | Protocol | `crates/bastion-protocol` | The API's types and routes, shared by the server and its clients. |"," | Server | `crates/bastion-server` | The HTTP API and its events, the factory, the store, the gate, the audit and the stack. |"," | Engine adapter | `crates/bastion-server/src/engine/` | The only server code that imports `iii-sdk`. |","+| Client library | `crates/bastion-client` | What every client uses to reach a server: the server list, the local server's start, the calls and the event stream. |"," | Desktop client | `crates/bastion-desktop` | The pages, on iced. |","+| Command line | `crates/bastion-cli` | `bastion`: list and follow jobs, submit a request, approve, send back, stop, update. |"," | Workers | `workers/` | Bastion's own iii workers. |"," "," `scripts/check-seams.sh` fails the build when code crosses a seam (DECISIONS.md"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/README.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"fec8eab1-a2fb-477d-8320-c80dedc06f51","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":41,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"38ce2c27-3654-4b44-afc7-30d85c6a7a43","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
