{"parentUuid":"9f619d36-fa08-414c-a72c-f3115bb35b76","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6cdd044d-0af5-4607-b3c2-163d5cb0b235","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Your questions have been answered: \"How far should the \"Bastion stage\" concept go away?\"=\"Remove it fully\". You can now continue with these answers in mind.","tool_use_id":"toolu_015MueXSBcsp92VWtmXKWE52"}]},"uuid":"bd5bc061-8bc7-4126-a232-8d6df5c18645","timestamp":"2026-11-11T18:43:23.667Z","toolUseResult":{"questions":[{"question":"How far should the \"Bastion stage\" concept go away?","header":"Stages","options":[{"label":"Hide it in the UI (Recommended)","description":"Everything reads as a series of steps. \"Runs as\" lists Prompt, Agent, Skill, Command, Shell, then named steps such as Plan, Build, Land or Merge, with no \"Bastion stage\" label. The engine keeps them, so land and merge stay safe. Small change."},{"label":"Agent stages become prompts","description":"Plan, build, review and the rest become plain prompt steps that start with the built-in text. Only actions such as Land, Ship, Merge, CI and Deploy stay special. Plan-to-build handoff, scope splits and specify's tests need rework. Large change."},{"label":"Remove it fully","description":"Every step is a prompt, agent, skill, command or shell script, and landing is a shell script you write. The PR, merge and gate safety Bastion gives today goes away. Very large change."}],"multiSelect":false}],"answers":{"How far should the \"Bastion stage\" concept go away?":"Remove it fully"},"annotations":{}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e668d70c-aa72-425b-8141-68f557fcb3d0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remote