{"parentUuid":"268282df-c3a2-4ebc-a3da-4c25c86edb42","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwdjip7YdYiW4P3QxRQU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G5E1nU6y6PzKnLTJ8dV7No","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"Pushing, opening a PR and merging need the network and Git credentials. Shell steps run in an offline VM today. Where should a landing script run?","header":"Landing","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"VM, network opt-in (Recommended)","description":"A shell step can tick \"needs network\". It then runs in a VM with the network, and with the credentials you name (such as GH_TOKEN) from the vault. Agent-written code still never runs on your machine."},{"label":"On the host","description":"The script runs on the server's machine as the server's user, with its git and gh logins. Simplest, but code from the job's branch can then run on your machine."},{"label":"Keep land built in","description":"Everything else becomes steps, but landing (merge into the branch, or push and open a PR) stays one built-in step kind."}]},{"question":"How should the work be split?","header":"Plan","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Phases, each shippable (Recommended)","description":"1: the new step model and runner beside the old one. 2: move the built-in workflows to steps. 3: re-key governance, dials and notices. 4: delete the stage code and its features. Each phase passes CI and is checked live before the next."},{"label":"One rewrite","description":"Replace the core in one go. It is faster to finish, but nothing works until all of it does."}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1416,"cache_read_input_tokens":535168,"output_tokens":1622,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1103},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_r