{"parentUuid":"8c1e6320-d42b-4049-a4bf-df051709a32a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6cdd044d-0af5-4607-b3c2-163d5cb0b235","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013tKgBQRzMFeoXFCBPVKCj9","type":"tool_result","content":"commit d7ec6e88c929e56e79bb5bfe852e4fe1841be33a\nAuthor: Ian Johnson <tacoda@hey.com>\nDate:   Mon Nov 9 17:24:34 2026 -0600\n\n    A second Bastion process on one stack gets its engine link\n    \n    The engine refuses a second worker named bastion-app, so the live tests,\n    and any second server or tool on the same stack, never linked while a\n    server ran. The worker name now carries the process id. The live tests\n    wait at most 15 s for the link and look for the checkout two levels up,\n    where it has been since the crates moved under crates/.\n    \n    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M71A1DSR9803CX7R67CC4KCE\n\n crates/bastion-server/src/doctor.rs     | 2 +-\n crates/bastion-server/src/engine/iii.rs | 2 +-\n crates/bastion-server/src/stack.rs      | 2 +-\n crates/bastion-server/src/store.rs      | 6 +++++-\n 4 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)\n33-     pub fn connect(url: &str) -> Self {\n34-         let options = InitOptions {\n35-             metadata: Some(WorkerMetadata {\n36:-                name: \"bastion-app\".into(),\n37:+                name: format!(\"bastion-app-{}\", std::process::id()),\n38-                 ..WorkerMetadata::default()\n39-             }),\n40-             namespace: Some(\"bastion\".into()),","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"dc1ddf88-2a24-4c30-84da-2c9ddfb3050d","timestamp":"2026-11-11T18:52:42.443Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"commit d7ec6e88c929e56e79bb5bfe852e4fe1841be33a\nAuthor: Ian Johnson <tacoda@hey.com>\nDate:   Mon Nov 9 17:24:34 2026 -0600\n\n    A second Bastion process on one stack gets its engine link\n    \n    The engine refuses a second worker named bastion-app, so the live tests,\n    and any second server or tool on the same stack, never linked while a\n   