{"parentUuid":"67a36c6c-031c-431e-a2b0-fe4d019bba5b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwoFyhCDPxoFZmeFhQL7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1117,"cache_read_input_tokens":724680,"output_tokens":742,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":129},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1117,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":742,"cache_read_input_tokens":724680,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1117,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1117},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5c4d29e1-5f65-4d3e-9d84-6b1b67973cd0","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwoFyMcBoUDEvwLp4k9A","type":"assistant","uuid":"ef436220-383c-4bd4-9677-ba8b732634e0","timestamp":"2026-11-11T20:48:42.671Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"ef436220-383c-4bd4-9677-ba8b732634e0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwoFyhCDPxoFZmeFhQL7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the vision as `VISION.md` and committed it on its own (`f6afb82`). The README and CLAUDE.md now point to it.\n\nIt records what you said:\n- **Purpose:** one desktop app where a developer runs jobs through factories, local, remote, or both, and defines each factory's workflows, capabilities and constraints. Common workflows come seeded with their text filled in, and every step stays editable.\n- **Two levels:**\n  - The Jobs pages span every server, filtered by server and workspace, and stay as they are.\n  - Every other page, Settings included, belongs to the server picked at the top, and never mixes two servers.\n- **What a server holds:** its workspaces, workflows, capabilities and constraints, settings (providers, people, notifications, secrets), and records. The only thing the app itself keeps is your list of servers.\n- **Local and remote:** a local server needs no credentials, and a remote one needs a token over TLS. Both run the same factory.\n- **Fixed:** agent code never runs on your machine, every action names its actor, and a seeded default never locks you in.\n\nThat points at the first page-by-page gap. Today's Settings page puts your server list and the server's workspaces in one \"places\" section. By the vision, the server list belongs to the app and workspaces belong to the server.\n\nS2 is still in flight:\n- **Short:** landed a change on `demo-local`, so that part of S2's live check passes.\n- **Pull request:** planned, built, passed its checks and opened [PR #3](https://github.com/ianparo/bastion-demo/pull/3). Its CI step hit the sandbox's 5-minute limit while GitHub's runner sat queued. I changed the CI script to wait 4.5 minutes and then ask for a retry.\n\nI'm waiting for that GitHub run to finish. Then I'll retry the step, let it merge, and commit S2."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1117,"cache_read_input_tokens":724680,"output_tokens":742,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":129},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1117,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":742,"cache_read_input_tokens":724680,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1117,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1117},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5c4d29e1-5f65-4d3e-9d84-6b1b67973cd0","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwoFyMcBoUDEvwLp4k9A","type":"assistant","uuid":"36d941c4-517a-4937-b18d-35d5f814592c","timestamp":"2026-11-11T20:48:42.689Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
