{"parentUuid":"757ef788-dcad-445c-b56f-a62c0a905b73","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwpYENYhYJFZf3amkpCN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DrrSe1HGrA8bgirpVrcvh1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\na='### S4. The stage code goes'\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,'''Done 2026-11-11, in part. An agent's step can only read: the gate refuses\nits file writes, and the seeded planning and criteria steps read only. A\nnotice names a workflow's step. Live: a read-only prompt told to write\n`NOTES.md` on `demo-local` was refused, and the audit log reads \"deny\n(This step only reads: it may not write a file.) sandbox::fs::write\n/work/repo/NOTES.md\". The settings' dials per stage and the evals' arms\nper stage move to S4, as they reach only the stage code it deletes.\n\n'''+a)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add PLAN.md && git commit -q -m \"S3: an agent's step can only read, and a notice names its step\n\nA workflow's prompt, agent, skill or command step can be marked as\nreading only (D42): the turn carries it to the gate, which refuses the\nstep's file writes whatever its kind's grants allow, and the audit keeps\nthe refusal. The shipped planning and criteria steps read only, and so\ndoes a seeded plan turned into steps. A notice names a workflow's step,\nnot its kind. The workflow editor marks a step as reading only.\" && git add VISION.md && git commit -q -m \"The vision: a server's settings are live controls over how iii behaves\" && git log --oneline -3","description":"Commit S3 and the vision update"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1496,"cache_read_input_tokens":755049,"output_tokens":594,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_request