{"parentUuid":"f0f0678b-788e-4759-97eb-f6a9cb9cf39b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwphoXqr2tLpHWPmzB2a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pushed: `origin/main` is at `875a965`.\n\nBefore S4, a warning: only 2.0 GB of disk is free. Last time the disk filled, every tool failed with `ENOSPC`. S4 rebuilds the whole workspace many times as it deletes code, and Rust builds here can use more than that. Please free more space first, for example:\n\n```\n! cargo clean --manifest-path /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/Cargo.toml\n```\n\nDeleting `data/observability`, the dev stack's traces (836 MB when I last checked), also helps if you don't need them.\n\nS4 is the largest phase: stages are referenced 556 times in 38 files. I'll split it into commits that each pass CI on their own:\n1. **Features that read a stage's output:** scope splits, discover questions, the acceptance-test machinery, UAT sign-off, learn, escapes, and the CI and deploy watches. This includes the Learning and Verification pages.\n2. **Built-in pipelines and stage briefs:** the code chains, the per-stage briefs, the per-stage dials in Settings, and the per-stage eval arms.\n3. **The stage set:** `Stage` shrinks to the five kinds. A migration moves stored jobs, artifacts and workflows to steps. Old stage names on finished jobs map to `prompt` or `shell`, and that loses the old labels.\n4. **The documents:** DECISIONS.md marks each replaced decision, and the README describes Bastion as it is now.\n\nTell me when there is room, and I'll start with commit 1."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":220,"cache_read_input_tokens":757913,"output_tokens":1377,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":858},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens"