"no VM\")?, &script).await;","+            if let Some(own) = &own {","+                self.stop_vm(own).await;","+            }","+            ran","+        };","+        ran.await","+            .unwrap_or_else(|detail: String| Event::StepStuck { detail })","+    }","+","+    /// Run `script` by sh in the VM's repository.","+    async fn script(&self, sandbox: &str, script: &str) -> Result<Event, String> {","+        let argv = [\"sh\", \"-c\", &format!(\"cd {REPO} && {script}\")];","+        let exec = json!({ \"sandbox_id\": sandbox, \"argv\": argv, \"timeout_ms\": SCRIPT_SECS * 1000 });","+        let wait = SCRIPT_SECS * 1000 + 60_000;","+        let out = self","+            .engine","+            .call_for(DEFAULT_NAMESPACE, \"sandbox::exec\", exec, wait)","+            .await?;","+        let printed = format!(","+            \"{}{}\",","+            out[\"stdout\"].as_str().unwrap_or_default(),","+            out[\"stderr\"].as_str().unwrap_or_default()","+        );","+        Ok(exited(out[\"exit_code\"].as_i64().unwrap_or(-1), tail(&printed)))","+    }","+","     /// The line a script starts with: `BASTION_BRANCH`, the job's branch;","     /// `BASTION_BASE`, the workspace's; `BASTION_REPO`, its GitHub","     /// `owner/name`, empty without an `origin`; `BASTION_CHECKS`, the"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-server/src/factory/split.rs","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":37,"newStart":0,"newLines":0,"lines":["-//! Scope split a request: keep each later part as a queued job,","-//! asked for by the same person on the same workflow. Admission holds each","-//! part until the one before it lands.","-","-use std::sync::Arc;","-","-use bastion_core::Job;","-","-use super::{Factory, now};","-use crate::store::{Record, Runtime};","-","-impl Factory {","-    pub(super) async fn add_parts(","-        self: &Arc<Self>,","-        of: &Record,","-        parts: Vec<Job>,","-    ) -> Result<(), String> {","-        for job in parts {","-            let id = job.id.clone();","-            let record = Record {","-                job,","-                runtime: Runtime {","-                    requester: of.runtime.requester.clone(),","-                    model: of.runtime.model.clone(),","-                    workflow: of.runtime.workflow.clone(),","-                    workflow_version: of.runtime.workflow_version,","-                    ..Runtime::default()","-                },","-                rev: 1,","-                created_at: now(),","-            };","-            self.store.insert(&record).await?;","-            self.changed(&id);","-        }","-        Ok(())","-    }","-}"]}],"deleted":true},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-server/src/factory/verdict.rs","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":130,"newStart":0,"newLines":0,"lines":["-//! A machine verdict on promotion. A repository that commits a","-//! `verify.yaml` contract has each change judged by opengantry's","-//! `gantry-verify` before it is pushed or landed. The verify runs the","-//! contract's checks, which run the agent's code, so it runs in a VM of its","-//! own with no network, never on the host. It reads the contract from the","-//! fork point, so a change cannot weaken the contract it is judged by.","-","-use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};","-","-use bastion_core::gates::parse;","-use bastion_core::{BASE_TAG, eval};","-","-use super::setup::{self, TREE};","-use super::{Factory, REPO};","-use crate::store::Record;","-","-/// The opengantry verify package, pinned.","-const KIT: &str = \"@jeger-ai/opengantry-verify@4.0.2\";","-/// Where the package's bin sits once its tarball is unpacked in a VM.","-const VERIFY: &str = \"/work/kit/node_modules/@jeger-ai/opengantry-verify/dist/cli.js\";","-/// The contract a repository commits to ask for a verdict.","-const CONTRACT: &str = \"verify.yaml\";","-","-impl Factory {","-    /// The verdict on the job's change, when its repository has a contract","-    /// at the fork point; an error says why the change may not go on.","-    pub(super) async fn verdict(&self, record: &Record) -> Result<bool, String> {","-        let vm = record.runtime.sandbox.as_deref().ok_or(\"no VM\")?;","-        let at_base = format!(\"{BASE_TAG}:{CONTRACT}\");","-        let contract = self","-            .vm_exec(vm, &[\"git\", \"-C\", REPO, \"show\", &at_base])","-            .await;","-        let empty = |out: &serde_json::Value| out[\"stdout\"].as_str().is_none_or(str::is_empty);","-        if contract.as_ref().is_ok_and(|c| !empty(c)) {","-            return self.judge(record, vm).await.map(|()| true);","-        }","-        Ok(false)","-    }","-","-    /// A trial's contract as a grader: the workspace's gates over the","-    /// change, with no autofix, then opengantry's verdict. None when the","-    /// workspace has no gates and the repository no contract.","-    pub(super) async fn contract_holds(&self, record: &Record) -> Result<Option<bool>, String> {","-        let vm = record.runtime.sandbox.as_deref().ok_or(\"no VM\")?;","-        let gates = parse(&self.workspace(record).await?.gates);","-        let files = self.changed_files(vm).await?;","-        let failed = match files.is_empty() {","-            true => Vec::new(),","-            false => self.failing(vm, &gates, &files).await,","-        };","-        let judged = self.verdict(record).await;","-        Ok(eval::contract(!gates.is_empty(), failed.is_empty(), judged))","-    }","-","-    /// Judge the change in a VM of its own, from the node image, offline.","-    async fn judge(&self, record: &Record, vm: &str) -> Result<(), String> {","-        let tree = self.tree(vm).await?;","-        let kit = self.verify_kit()?;","-        let ws = self.workspace(record).await?;","-        let judge = self","-            .create_vm_from(\"node\", &ws, setup::Access::network(false))","-            .await?;","-        let judged = self.judge_in(&judge, tree, kit).await;","-        self.stop_vm(&judge).await;","-        judged.map_err(|e| format!(\"opengantry refused the change ({CONTRACT}):\\n{e}\"))","-    }","-","-    /// Unpack the tree and the verify package in `vm`, and run the verify.","-    async fn judge_in(&self, vm: &str, tree: Vec<u8>, kit: Vec<u8>) -> Result<(), String> {","-        self.put(vm, TREE, tree).await?;","-        self.vm_exec(vm, &[\"tar\", \"xzf\", TREE, \"-C\", \"/work\"])","-            .await?;","-        self.put(vm, \"/work/kit.tgz\", kit).await?;","-        self.vm_exec(vm, &[\"mkdir\", \"-p\", \"/work/kit\"]).await?;","-        self.vm_exec(vm, &[\"tar\", \"xzf\", \"/work/kit.tgz\", \"-C\", \"/work/kit\"])","-            .await?;","-        self.run_in_repo(vm, &format!(\"node {VERIFY} --base {BASE_TAG}\"))","-            .await","-    }","-","-    /// The verify package and what it needs, as a tarball, installed on the","-    /// host once with no install scripts.","-    fn verify_kit(&self) -> Result<Vec<u8>, String> {","-        let dir = kit_dir(&self.scratch);","-        let tarball = dir.join(\"kit.tgz\");","-        if self.machine.exists(&tarball) {","-            return self.machine.read_bytes(&tarball);","-        }","-        self.machine.make_dir(&dir)?;","-        let at = dir.display().to_string();","-        let install = [","-            \"install\",","-            \"--prefix\",","-            &at,","-            \"--ignore-scripts\",","-            \"--no-audit\",","-            \"--no-fund\",","-            KIT,","-        ];","-        self.host(\"npm\", &install, &dir)?;","-        let file = tarball.display().to_string();","-        self.host(\"tar\", &[\"czf\", &file, \"-C\", &at, \"node_modules\"], &dir)?;","-        self.machine.read_bytes(&tarball)","-    }","-","-    fn host(&self, program: &str, args: &[&str], dir: &Path) -> Result<(), String> {","-        let out = self.machine.run(program, args, Some(dir))?;","-        match out.success {","-            true => Ok(()),","-            false => Err(format!(\"{program} {}: {}\", args[0], out.text.trim())),","-        }","-    }","-}","-","-/// Where the verify package is kept, by its pinned version.","-fn kit_dir(scratch: &Path) -> PathBuf {","-    let version = KIT.rsplit('@').next().unwrap_or_default();","-    scratch.join(format!(\"opengantry-verify-{version}\"))","-}","-","-#[cfg(test)]","-mod tests {","-    use super::*;","-","-    #[test]","-    fn the_kit_is_kept_by_its_pinned_version() {","-        let dir = kit_dir(Path::new(\"/scratch\"));","-        assert_eq!(dir, Path::new(\"/scratch/opengantry-verify-4.0.2\"));","-    }","-}"]}],"deleted":true}],"moreFiles":1,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-server/src/factory/acceptance.rs","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-server/src/factory/gates.rs","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-server/src/factory/shell.rs","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-server/src/factory/split.rs","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-server/src/factory/verdict.rs","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-server/src/spec.rs"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e8cb3df1-4936-4617-b0d6-854c50a3c697","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":6,"modified":10,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8d8b2e53-5f85-47cc-98ea-68d4ee0a444f","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
