 and adding the server in the desktop app's Settings.\n9. Model provider keys and GH_TOKEN go into the server's vault from the app, never in files.\n10. Backups of the server's data folder, and updating with `bastion update`.\n11. A short \"what can go wrong\" list with the fix for each.\n\nRules for the document:\n- Write it to /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/docs/hosting/hetzner.md. Create the folder. Do not commit, and do not touch any other file.\n- Plain, simplified technical English: one idea per sentence, active voice, imperative steps, no em dashes, sentence-case headings, American spelling.\n- Never invent a flag, a port, or a price. If the code or a source does not settle a fact, write it as an open question.\n- Mark each fact from the web with its source URL.\n\nReply with a short summary: the machine you recommend and why, the ports, how TLS works for this server, and the open questions.","run_in_background":"true"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5c7d2d7f-5e59-485e-82f4-6d68f3410599","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgwqwJUcpyALDzjre98kP","type":"assistant","uuid":"f8780fcd-75ed-4457-8f24-010ac0222acd","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:24:03.949Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
