plets do not support nested virtualization. Confirm what is true now and cite the source URLs. If no DigitalOcean product can run the sandbox, say so plainly in the first section, and then give the best workable option (for example: run the Bastion server on a Droplet only if the sandbox can run elsewhere, which you must check in the code; or name the closest provider that would work). Do not pretend a setup works.\n\nThe plan must cover, as numbered steps with exact commands, for the option that works:\n1. Team account and project for work use, SSH key, and the machine to create (type, region, rough monthly price, with source).\n2. Ubuntu version and first hardening: a non-root user, SSH keys only, unattended upgrades.\n3. Checking /dev/kvm and virtualization before anything else.\n4. Installing `iii` 0.25.0 and any other dependency the stack needs (find them in the repo).\n5. Installing bastion-server with scripts/install.sh `--service` (the curl install command the README gives), and enabling lingering for the systemd user service.\n6. A DNS name (DigitalOcean DNS is fine) and a TLS certificate: Let's Encrypt with certbot, or a reverse proxy such as Caddy if the server's own TLS cannot take a renewing certificate; decide from the code. Renewal.\n7. Firewall: a DigitalOcean Cloud Firewall and ufw. Open only SSH and the server's HTTPS port; say which ports the iii engine and workers use, and that they must stay closed to the internet.\n8. Giving the owner a token for the remote server, and adding the server in the desktop app's Settings.\n9. Model provider keys and GH_TOKEN go into the server's vault from the app, never in files.\n10. Backups (snapshots and the server's data folder), and updating with `bastion update`.\n11. A short \"what can go wrong\" list with the fix for each.\n\nRules for the document:\n- Write it to /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/docs/hosting/digitalocean.md. Create the folder if needed. Do not commit, and do not touch any other file.\n- Plain, simplified technical English: one idea per sentence, active voice, imperative steps, no em dashes, sentence-case headings, American spelling.\n- Never invent a flag, a port, or a price. If the code or a source does not settle a fact, write it as an open question.\n- Mark each fact from the web with its source URL.\n\nReply with a short summary: whether DigitalOcean can run it and on what, the ports, how TLS works for this server, and the open questions.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1987,"cache_read_input_tokens":908227,"output_tokens":3582,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":497},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1987,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3582,"cache_read_input_tokens":908227,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1987,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1987},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LEujiZBhSXV33ojJ7fZxx3":{"description":"DigitalOcean hosting plan for bastion-server","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Write a plan for installing and running `bastion-server` on DigitalOcean with Ubuntu, reachable remotely over TLS, so the Bastion desktop app on a Mac can attach to it as a remote server. The owner's employer uses DigitalOcean, and this would hold their work accounts, so note anything about team accounts, projects and billing separation.\n\nContext you must read first, in /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion (a Rust workspace):\n- README.md, VISION.md, DECISIONS.md (especially D30, D31: remote servers, people, tokens, TLS).\n- scripts/install.s