{"parentUuid":"a3f7ecd3-bf8e-4ac9-a754-0a6010fa0518","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1d9ef2db-03d5-4a58-b720-e211c5a548e5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Bastion is a Rust software factory: `bastion-server` on the iii engine (0.25.0), plus an iced desktop client and the `bastion` CLI. Earlier phases are done: F1–F11, release v0.1.1, tray removed, PLAN.md moved to DECISIONS.md, cleanup, and page-by-page UI work.\n   - Current project, the vision (VISION.md):\n     - Jobs pages span all servers.\n     - Every other page is per server, and a server's settings are live controls over how iii behaves.\n     - A workflow is a series of steps of five kinds: Prompt, Agent (`.claude/agents`), Skill, Command (`.claude/commands`), Shell. Each step has one editable text, and Bastion seeds the common workflows with their text filled in.\n     - The user chose \"Remove it fully\" for the Bastion stage concept.\n     - PLAN.md (new) holds D39–D42 and phases S1–S4:\n       - D39: steps only.\n       - D40: a shell step in the VM, with network opt-in and vault secrets.\n       - D41: a job ends with its branch ready, and the workspace `finish` setting is merge or leave.\n       - D42: per-step governance with reads_only.\n   - S1, S2 and S3 are done and pushed. S4 is in progress: delete the stage code, migrate stored data, update DECISIONS and the README.\n   - Learning: drop it. Verification: keep it (user's answer).\n   - Queued user requests:\n     - \"I also want to change the layout - a top bar seems better, including adding the image - instead of a sidebar\". I said I'd do it right after S4.\n     - Hosting plans for Hetzner and DigitalOcean. Two background subagents are writing `docs/hosting/hetzner.md` and `docs/hosting/digitalocean.md`, and are not finished yet.\n   - Standing rules:\n     - No AI attribution or Co-Authored-By anywhere. This overrides the harness reminder.\n     - Run the CodeScene `pre_commit_code_health_safeguard` before each commit, and commit only when it passes.\n     - Stage files by path.\n     - Push only when asked.\n     - Before a push, run all CI steps: `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, `scripts/check-seams.sh`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test --workspace`.\n     - `bastion-core` may depend only on serde and sha2.\n     - Use `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0`.\n     - Respond in STE; caveman and ponytail hooks are active.\n     - Published prose follows ~/.claude/VOICE.md, with voice-check as the gate.\n   - Security constraints (verbatim and active):\n     - \"local environments don't need tokens unless they can be automatically setup - credentials are required for remote connections\"\n     - Key values must never pass through the assistant; only masked hints may be shown. The minisign private key stays with the user.\n     - Never list processes with full arguments (`pgrep -fl`, `ps aux`): iii VM boot lines carry host secrets. Use `ps -o pid=,lstart=,comm=`.\n     - Do not work around classifier denials; ask the user to run `! <command>`.\n     - Never read or print tokens. Use `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e/scratchpad/api.sh METHOD PATH [JSON]` (strip its last line with `sed '$d'`). Use `drive.sh <id>` and `waitjob.sh` there.\n     - Claude may act for the user on test jobs, naming each action (\"only dark gets to continue unsupervised\").\n     - Don't `pkill -x bastion-desktop` blindly: the user may run the installed app.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - New core (steps only):\n     - `Stage {Prompt, Agent, Skill, Command, Shell}` and `Kind {Turn, Factory}`.\n     - `Job` fields: id, workspace, request, stage, state, question, feedback, failures, error, updated_at, revisions (`BTreeMap<String step id, u32>`), last_refusal, flow, node, results.\n     - `node == None` with a non-empty flow means `finishing()`.\n     - `Bounds {trial, revision_budget}` replaces `Dials`. Per-step dials come from the nodes.\n     - Events: Admitted, Provisioned, ProvisionFailed, TurnFinished, Approved, Commented, Landed, LandFailed, Stopped, Ran, StepFailed, StepStuck, VmLost, Retried, Extended.\n     - Effects: Provision, StartTurn, RecordArtifact, CaptureDiff, RunStep, Finish, Teardown, DarkDecided.\n     - A failing shell step sends its output to the nearest earlier non-read-only agent step (`fixer()`), at most `MAX_REVISIONS = 2` times and within the budget.\n     - A comment sends the work back to the fixer. A trial stops instead of finishing.\n     - `steps(job) -> Vec<(String, Stage, StepState)>`; `restart(job)` takes no dials.\n   - The workflow Reach struct: `{network, secrets, reads_only}`. `level_of(&[Dial])`. No chains and no landing check.\n   - Settings: `{plan_model, build_model, tracker, intake_paused}`. `model_for(reads_only, job_model)`. Dials, forge and Oversight are gone.\n   - `secrets.rs`: the secret detection kept from publish.rs.\n   - Migrations (`user_version`): every `rebuild()` maps old stage names to prompt or shell in the temp copy (`as_steps`). Old-stage capabilities are deleted, and jobs.back_to is set to NULL. Migration 5: `current` rebuild plus `nodes_as_steps()`:\n     - delete factory/checkpoint nodes and their links and results\n     - a reading stage becomes a reads_only prompt, its note prefixed \"Do not change any file. \"\n     - other agent stages become prompt\n   - `SqlStore::transaction` now errors when `committed: false`.\n   - The workflow version number counts past every kept version.\n   - Network shell step: a fresh VM with network and secret env, built through the `setup::Access {network, env}` struct.\n     - Vault read: `secrets::get` (consumers), then `secrets::access` adding `engine::worker_name()` (\"bastion-app-<pid>\"), then `secrets::resolve {ref}`, then restore the consumers. Namespace `bastion`.\n   - Shell scripts get `BASTION_BRANCH`, `BASTION_BASE`, `BASTION_REPO` and `BASTION_CHECKS`. The sandbox caps a command at 300 s.\n   - Shipped workflows live in seed_flows.rs (short, pull-request, full, full_no_acceptance). `DEFAULT_WORKFLOW = \"short\"`. `ships(id)`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (S4 work, mostly uncommitted):\n   - `crates/bastion-core/src/lib.rs`: fully rewritten as the steps-only state machine. Modules: audit, brief, charter, escape, eval, govern, media, notice, people, request, review, secrets, settings, workflow. Exports `brief`, `outcome`, `BASE_TAG`, `QUESTION_MARKER`, `results`.\n   - `crates/bastion-core/src/brief.rs`: rewritten. `intro` per kind, `brief`, `workflow_step`, `outcome`.\n   - `crates/bastion-core/src/settings.rs`: rewritten, with tests.\n   - `crates/bastion-core/src/workflow.rs`: chain, chain_id, custom and the landing check are removed; `level_of(dials)`; tests rewritten with a `prompt()` helper.\n   - `crates/bastion-core/src/notice.rs`: `entered` compares (state, node); text uses node or \"the finish\".\n   - `crates/bastion-core/src/secrets.rs`: new.\n   - `crates/bastion-core/src/tests.rs`: new state machine tests. 56 core tests pass.\n   - Deleted from core: acceptance.rs, gates.rs, pipeline.rs, publish.rs, full_tests.rs. Tests in govern, eval, charter and review were sed-mapped: Plan→Agent, Build→Prompt, Review→Shell.\n   - `crates/bastion-server/src/factory/land.rs`: reduced to finish_job, bring_back, land_here, keep_commits, fork_point, workspace.\n   - `crates/bastion-server/src/factory/shell.rs`:\n     - Added `shell_step`, `script` (300 s), `tail`, `exited`; `vault_value`; `networked_vm`.\n     - Added `shell_env`, which now includes `BASTION_CHECKS`.\n   - Deleted from the server: factory/acceptance.rs, gates.rs, verdict.rs, split.rs, spec.rs, learn.rs, api/learn.rs.\n   - `crates/bastion-server/src/factory.rs`:\n     - Submission without pipeline and criteria; submit and submit_trial run on `workflow_store::start_on(store, id, job)`.\n     - `bounds_for`; `DEFAULT_WORKFLOW`; `is_diff`/`NO_COMMITS`.\n     - Effect dispatch: `RunStep` goes to `run_step(record)`, which goes to `shell_step`. The CaptureDiff artifact uses `record.job.stage`.\n     - `tidy_after_turn` uses reads_only. check_contract and writes_code are removed, and `grade_trial` is unconditional.\n   - `crates/bastion-server/src/store/sql.rs`: `record()` and `job_params` map only the new fields, writing Null or defaults for old columns; save UPDATE trimmed; tasks removed.\n   - `crates/bastion-server/src/store/schema.rs`: rebuild with `as_steps`, `AGENT_STAGES`/`FACTORY_STAGES`, migration 5 with `nodes_as_steps()`.\n   - `crates/bastion-server/src/workflow_store.rs`: no BUILT_IN or chains. `ships()` delegates to `seed_flows::ships`; `all(store)`, `find(store, id)`, `start_on(store, id, job) -> (Job, u64)`. Its tests are still old.\n   - `crates/bastion-server/src/seed_flows.rs`: STAGED and `as_steps` removed; `ships()` added; the test is renamed.\n   - `seed/governance.sql`: capabilities are now only prompt, agent, skill and command allowed.\n   - Server API and handlers:\n     - settings_store, api/settings (presets gone, forge gone)\n     - api/govern (`factory_capabilities` rewritten with 3 rows), govern_store (dials removed)\n     - access (UAT sign-off removed; http approve uses `on_job`)\n     - decide (names node), onboard (`model_for(true)`, stage Prompt, reads_only metadata)\n     - resume (`restart(&record.job)`), reverts (`lands()` scans artifacts starting with `escape::COMMITS`)\n     - evals (diff by `is_diff`; reviewed is Stopped with a node)\n     - forge.rs (keeps only gh, slug_of, has_origin, slug, GitHub issues)\n     - http.rs (no pipeline, parts, dials or preset routes), turn.rs (no `usable`/spec)\n   - Protocol: removed ProposalView/Decision, SettingsPreset, SettingsView.forge, Dials routes and DialsView/PipelineDials/StepDial, JobParts, JobSubmit.pipeline, and JobSummary pr/parent/part/parts.\n   - Desktop: the learn page is removed so far (Route count 10, LEARN icon gone). It hasn't been updated for the other protocol changes yet.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - The first version of migration 4 dropped later job columns (dev DB data loss, disclosed). Fixed with JOB_COLUMNS via `current`.\n   - Silent DB transaction failures (`committed:false` read as success) are fixed. This revealed the version collision, which is fixed.\n   - The approved-finish bug left the job NeedsYou; fixed by setting Running.\n   - The result parser let a repeated empty header overwrite a result; fixed.\n   - The sandbox's 300 s exec cap: the CI script waits 270 s.\n   - CI apt hangs on ubuntu-latest (26.04): pinned to 24.04, with retries.\n   - Code Health failures, each fixed by extraction or simplification.\n   - Old-stage rows would break rebuilds on older DBs: fixed by mapping in `rebuild`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - S1 live: PR #2.\n   - S2 live: Short landed `negate`; Pull request merged PR #3 (CI was failing, and the user said merge).\n   - S3 live: a read-only write was refused and audited.\n   - Ongoing: the server compile on the new core.\n\n6. All user messages (this segment):\n   - \"continue\" (several times)\n   - \"Let's try again.\" / \"Red CI again\" / \"push\" / \"push first\" / \"push and continue\" / \"push and continue with S2\" / \"push, then we will start the page by page work Before we do take a look at the repository If there is anything out-of-date or leftover, clean it up.\"\n   - \"ok, take a look at the plan, If it's complete, delete it. I have another set of things to do and we will do those page by page.\"\n   - \"First, I want to get rid of the tray client - it's unnecessary and buggy\"\n   - \"We will start with the jobs page ... Quite a bit of the styling does not look good - especially the text. The hover effect is nice, but the container needs to stay visible.\"\n   - \"I also want a way to select multiple lines to comment on\"\n   - \"Try again / I quit all my bastion instances\"\n   - \"This error message is not helpful ... The plan section should be styled better and it should use ASD-STE100\"\n   - \"On the new request page, the workflow and kind values are redundant - only use workflow / Also layout the form in a nicer way to take advantage of horizontal space\"\n   - \"On the job page the workflow area is unnecessarily big\"\n   - \"push / I'm ready to move on to the next page\"\n   - \"Many workflows do not have information in them. I want to have the text readily avilable to edit. ... I'm also not a fan of the step split. I want each step to allow for editing text, whether that's a prompt, agent invocation, skill invocation, command invocation, shell script, or cli command.\"\n   - \"Replace dark with a moon icon and lights-on with a sun icon\"\n   - \"What is a bastion stage? I'm not sure if we need that concept - it should just be a series of steps\"\n   - \"I want the workflow to be fully definable and customizable with the pre-seeded information in place for the common workflows.\"\n   - \"Also the jobs pages should be able to filter on server in addition to workspace\"\n   - \"The title shouldn't be the type it is - it should be its title\"\n   - \"I stored the token, go ahead\"\n   - \"I freed up the space, continue\" (twice)\n   - \"IT's failing / Just merge and commit S2\"\n   - \"I want to create a vision for this product. It's pretty close. We still need to go page-by-page. I want the jobs pages to be as they are for now. All other pages, including settings, are for each server. Servers can be local or remote and have all their settings tied to them. The goal is to have a GUI application that a developer can use to run jobs through a factory server locally or remotely, or in combination, allow them to define their own workflows, capabilities, constraints, and so on\"\n   - \"The main idea is to allow users to dynamically adjust these values and it changes the way that iii works and behaves.\"\n   - \"I also want to change the layout - a top bar seems better, including adding the image - instead of a sidebar\"\n   - \"Also, I want to put this server on a hetzner server and host it to attach to including TLS. I still have to create a hetzner account. Create a subagent to write a plan to install the bastion-server on the VPS using Ubuntu along with any dependencies or additional setup required (such as certs and firewall ports, etc) Also do one for digital ocean - my job uses that and I think that would be a good place for my work accounts.\"\n   - AskUserQuestion answers: release v0.1.1; keep decisions file and keep open questions; full instructions, 5 kinds, shell override; remove stages fully; VM network opt-in and phases; workspace setting; keep Verification and drop Learning.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Finish S4:\n     - Fix the server compile (api/workflows.rs, api/factory imports).\n     - Remove `builtin` from NodeView and `built_in` from WorkflowView, in the protocol and the desktop.\n     - Rewrite or delete the stage-based server tests: factory/tests.rs, later_tests.rs, workflow_store tests, store tests, gate tests, and others.\n     - Update the desktop for the protocol changes: job page parts/UAT/PR, jobs families via parent, settings dials/forge/preset, workflows kinds and builtin, evals stage targets. Update the CLI if it uses pipeline.\n     - Run every CI step; run the safeguard.\n     - Live-check migration 5 on the dev DB (restart the server) and run a job.\n     - Commit. Update DECISIONS.md (mark replaced decisions, add D39–D42) and the README.\n     - Record S4 in PLAN.md.\n   - Then the top bar layout with the castle image, replacing the sidebar.\n   - Relay the Hetzner and DigitalOcean plan results when the subagents finish.\n   - Nothing from S4 is committed or pushed yet, except the learn removal (bbddad0, unpushed).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was fixing the last `bastion-server` compile errors after the core rewrite. The latest error list:\n   - api/factory.rs: unresolved imports `bastion_protocol::DialsView, PipelineDials, StepDial` in its `use bastion_protocol::{...}` line.\n   - api/workflows.rs:\n     - `bastion_core::instructions` (line 32, in `view_of`'s `builtin:` field)\n     - `w.built_in()` (line 18)\n     - `of_job` uses `settings_store::current(store).await?.dials` and `Graph::chain(&r.job.stages(), ...)`\n     - `every()` calls `workflow_store::all(store, &dials)`\n\n   Planned fixes:\n   - `view_of`: drop `built_in` and `builtin`, and remove those fields from the protocol `WorkflowView`/`NodeView` and the desktop (`workflows.rs` `shown`/`keep_text`/`builtin_of`/`text_label`).\n   - `of_job`: when there is no version, return `view_of(&Workflow { id, name, version: 0, graph: Graph::default() })`.\n   - `every(store)` becomes `workflow_store::all(store).await`.\n   - `workflow_delete`: when shipped, reseed via `seed_flows::seed`.\n   - Remove the unused `settings_store` import.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue the S4 server port exactly where I left off. The last action was reading `crates/bastion-server/src/api/workflows.rs`, after saying: \"I'm finishing the server's compile fixes: the workflow API is last. A step no longer has \"built-in\" instructions, because every step's text is its own now. So the `builtin` field and the workflow's `built_in` flag go from the protocol.\"\n\n   Next:\n   - Edit api/workflows.rs: `view_of` without `built_in`/`builtin`; `of_job` falls back to an empty graph; `every` uses `workflow_store::all(store)`.\n   - Fix the api/factory.rs imports.\n   - Remove the fields from the protocol.\n   - Rebuild until `cargo build -p bastion-server` passes, then move to the server tests and the desktop.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/tacoda/.claude/projects/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"98cb57e9-87f7-4fbf-b98a-70ba20833083","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:30:14.322Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":165,"turnIndex":260},"turnOrigin":"human","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"98cb57e9-87f7-4fbf-b98a-70ba20833083","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-server/src/forge.rs","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-server/src/forge.rs","content":"//! The GitHub tracker adapter (DECISIONS.md D23): a workspace's\n//! repository by its `origin`, the owner's account, and issues as\n//! requests, through the stock `github` worker's `gh`. Pull requests, CI\n//! and merges are a workflow's own shell steps now (D39).\n\nuse std::path::Path;\n\nuse serde_json::{Value, json};\n\nuse crate::engine::Engine;\nuse crate::engine::NS;\nuse crate::machine::Machine;\n\n/// Run `gh` through the github worker. A non-zero exit is an error with gh's stderr.\npub async fn gh(engine: &dyn Engine, args: &[&str]) -> Result<String, String> {\n    let out = engine\n        .call_for(NS, \"github::exec\", json!({ \"args\": args }), 120_000)\n        .await?;\n    match out[\"exit_code\"].as_i64() {\n        Some(0) => Ok(out[\"stdout\"].as_str().unwrap_or_default().to_string()),\n        _ => Err(format!(\n            \"gh {}: {}\",\n            args.join(\" \"),\n            out[\"stderr\"].as_str().unwrap_or_default().trim()\n        )),\n    }\n}\n\n/// `owner/name` from a GitHub remote URL, ssh or https.\npub fn slug_of(url: &str) -> Option<String> {\n    let rest = url\n        .trim()\n        .strip_prefix(\"git@github.com:\")\n        .or_else(|| url.trim().strip_prefix(\"https://github.com/\"))?;\n    let slug = rest.trim_end_matches('/').trim_end_matches(\".git\");\n    (slug.split('/').count() == 2).then(|| slug.to_string())\n}\n\n/// Whether a checkout has an `origin` remote to push to.\npub fn has_origin(machine: &dyn Machine, path: &Path) -> bool {\n    let out = machine.run(\"git\", &[\"remote\", \"get-url\", \"origin\"], Some(path));\n    out.is_ok_and(|o| o.success)\n}\n\n/// The GitHub repository a checkout's `origin` points at.\npub fn slug(machine: &dyn Machine, path: &Path) -> Result<String, String> {\n    let out = machine.run(\"git\", &[\"remote\", \"get-url\", \"origin\"], Some(path))?;\n    if !out.success {\n        return Err(format!(\"{} has no origin remote\", path.display()));\n    }\n    slug_of(&out.text).ok_or(format!(\n        \"origin is not a GitHub repository: {}\",\n        out.text.trim()\n    ))\n}\n\n/// One GitHub repository, reached through the github worker.\npub struct GitHub<'a> {\n    pub engine: &'a dyn Engine,\n    pub slug: String,\n}\n\nimpl GitHub<'_> {\n    async fn gh(&self, args: &[&str]) -> Result<String, String> {\n        let mut all = args.to_vec();\n        all.extend([\"--repo\", self.slug.as_str()]);\n        gh(self.engine, &all).await\n    }\n\n    pub async fn issues(&self) -> Result<Vec<Issue>, String> {\n        let out = self\n            .gh(&[\n                \"issue\",\n                \"list\",\n                \"--state\",\n                \"open\",\n                \"--json\",\n                \"number,title,body,url\",\n            ])\n            .await?;\n        let all: Value = serde_json::from_str(&out).map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n        Ok(all\n            .as_array()\n            .into_iter()\n            .flatten()\n            .filter_map(issue_of)\n            .collect())\n    }\n\n    pub async fn issue(&self, number: u64) -> Result<Issue, String> {\n        let n = number.to_string();\n        let out = self\n            .gh(&[\"issue\", \"view\", &n, \"--json\", \"number,title,body,url\"])\n            .await?;\n        serde_json::from_str::<Value>(&out)\n            .ok()\n            .as_ref()\n            .and_then(issue_of)\n            .ok_or(format!(\"issue {number} did not read\"))\n    }\n}\n\n/// One issue as a request source.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct Issue {\n    pub number: u64,\n    pub title: String,\n    pub body: String,\n    pub url: String,\n}\n\nfn issue_of(v: &Value) -> Option<Issue> {\n    Some(Issue {\n        number: v[\"number\"].as_u64()?,\n        title: v[\"title\"].as_str()?.into(),\n        body: v[\"body\"].as_str().unwrap_or_default().into(),\n        url: v[\"url\"].as_str()?.into(),\n    })\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n\n    #[test]\n    fn a_checkout_has_an_origin_only_when_git_names_one() {\n        let at = Path::new(\"/repo\");\n        let named = crate::machine::fake::FakeMachine::new().run_ok(\"git\", \"git@github.com:a/b\");\n        assert!(has_origin(&named, at));\n        let none = crate::machine::fake::FakeMachine::new().run_fails(\"git\", \"No such remote\");\n        assert!(!has_origin(&none, at));\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn a_remote_url_gives_its_slug() {\n        assert_eq!(\n            slug_of(\"git@github.com:ianparo/bastion.git\\n\"),\n            Some(\"ianparo/bastion\".into())\n        );\n        assert_eq!(\n            slug_of(\"https://github.com/ianparo/bastion\"),\n            Some(\"ianparo/bastion\".into())\n        );\n        assert_eq!(slug_of(\"git@gitlab.com:o/r.git\"), None);\n        assert_eq!(slug_of(\"/tmp/demo-a\"), None);\n    }\n}\n","numLines":148,"startLine":1,"totalLines":148}},"displayPath":"crates/bastion-server/src/forge.rs"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3fe8b5c7-b534-47b0-a83b-29a127506743","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:30:14.583Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-server/src/forge.rs\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t//! The GitHub tracker adapter (DECISIONS.md D23): a workspace's\n2\t//! repository by its `origin`, the owner's account, and issues as\n3\t//! requests, through the stock `github` worker's `gh`. Pull requests, CI\n4\t//! and merges are a workflow's own shell steps now (D39).\n5\t\n6\tuse std::path::Path;\n7\t\n8\tuse serde_json::{Value, json};\n9\t\n10\tuse crate::engine::Engine;\n11\tuse crate::engine::NS;\n12\tuse crate::machine::Machine;\n13\t\n14\t/// Run `gh` through the github worker. A non-zero exit is an error with gh's stderr.\n15\tpub async fn gh(engine: &dyn Engine, args: &[&str]) -> Result<String, String> {\n16\t    let out = engine\n17\t        .call_for(NS, \"github::exec\", json!({ \"args\": args }), 120_000)\n18\t        .await?;\n19\t    match out[\"exit_code\"].as_i64() {\n20\t        Some(0) => Ok(out[\"stdout\"].as_str().unwrap_or_default().to_string()),\n21\t        _ => Err(format!(\n22\t            \"gh {}: {}\",\n23\t            args.join(\" \"),\n24\t            out[\"stderr\"].as_str().unwrap_or_default().trim()\n25\t        )),\n26\t    }\n27\t}\n28\t\n29\t/// `owner/name` from a GitHub remote URL, ssh or https.\n30\tpub fn slug_of(url: &str) -> Option<String> {\n31\t    let rest = url\n32\t        .trim()\n33\t        .strip_prefix(\"git@github.com:\")\n34\t        .or_else(|| url.trim().strip_prefix(\"https://github.com/\"))?;\n35\t    let slug = rest.trim_end_matches('/').trim_end_matches(\".git\");\n36\t    (slug.split('/').count() == 2).then(|| slug.to_string())\n37\t}\n38\t\n39\t/// Whether a checkout has an `origin` remote to push to.\n40\tpub fn has_origin(machine: &dyn Machine, path: &Path) -> bool {\n41\t    let out = machine.run(\"git\", &[\"remote\", \"get-url\", \"origin\"], Some(path));\n42\t    out.is_ok_and(|o| o.success)\n43\t}\n44\t\n45\t/// The GitHub repository a checkout's `origin` points at.\n46\tpub fn slug(machine: &dyn Machine, path: &Path) -> Result<String, String> {\n47\t    let out = machine.run(\"git\", &[\"remote\", \"get-url\", \"origin\"], Some(path))?;\n48\t    if !out.success {\n49\t        return Err(format!(\"{} has no origin remote\", path.display()));\n50\t    }\n51\t    slug_of(&out.text).ok_or(format!(\n52\t        \"origin is not a GitHub repository: {}\",\n53\t        out.text.trim()\n54\t    ))\n55\t}\n56\t\n57\t/// One GitHub repository, reached through the github worker.\n58\tpub struct GitHub<'a> {\n59\t    pub engine: &'a dyn Engine,\n60\t    pub slug: String,\n61\t}\n62\t\n63\timpl GitHub<'_> {\n64\t    async fn gh(&self, args: &[&str]) -> Result<String, String> {\n65\t        let mut all = args.to_vec();\n66\t        all.extend([\"--repo\", self.slug.as_str()]);\n67\t        gh(self.engine, &all).await\n68\t    }\n69\t\n70\t    pub async fn issues(&self) -> Result<Vec<Issue>, String> {\n71\t        let out = self\n72\t            .gh(&[\n73\t                \"issue\",\n74\t                \"list\",\n75\t                \"--state\",\n76\t                \"open\",\n77\t                \"--json\",\n78\t                \"number,title,body,url\",\n79\t            ])\n80\t            .await?;\n81\t        let all: Value = serde_json::from_str(&out).map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n82\t        Ok(all\n83\t            .as_array()\n84\t            .into_iter()\n85\t            .flatten()\n86\t            .filter_map(issue_of)\n87\t            .collect())\n88\t    }\n89\t\n90\t    pub async fn issue(&self, number: u64) -> Result<Issue, String> {\n91\t        let n = number.to_string();\n92\t        let out = self\n93\t            .gh(&[\"issue\", \"view\", &n, \"--json\", \"number,title,body,url\"])\n94\t            .await?;\n95\t        serde_json::from_str::<Value>(&out)\n96\t            .ok()\n97\t            .as_ref()\n98\t            .and_then(issue_of)\n99\t            .ok_or(format!(\"issue {number} did not read\"))\n100\t    }\n101\t}\n102\t\n103\t/// One issue as a request source.\n104\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\n105\tpub struct Issue {\n106\t    pub number: u64,\n107\t    pub title: String,\n108\t    pub body: String,\n109\t    pub url: String,\n110\t}\n111\t\n112\tfn issue_of(v: &Value) -> Option<Issue> {\n113\t    Some(Issue {\n114\t        number: v[\"number\"].as_u64()?,\n115\t        title: v[\"title\"].as_str()?.into(),\n116\t        body: v[\"body\"].as_str().unwrap_or_default().into(),\n117\t        url: v[\"url\"].as_str()?.into(),\n118\t    })\n119\t}\n120\t\n121\t#[cfg(test)]\n122\tmod tests {\n123\t    use super::*;\n124\t\n125\t    #[test]\n126\t    fn a_checkout_has_an_origin_only_when_git_names_one() {\n127\t        let at = Path::new(\"/repo\");\n128\t        let named = crate::machine::fake::FakeMachine::new().run_ok(\"git\", \"git@github.com:a/b\");\n129\t        assert!(has_origin(&named, at));\n130\t        let none = crate::machine::fake::FakeMachine::new().run_fails(\"git\", \"No such remote\");\n131\t        assert!(!has_origin(&none, at));\n132\t    }\n133\t\n134\t    #[test]\n135\t    fn a_remote_url_gives_its_slug() {\n136\t        assert_eq!(\n137\t            slug_of(\"git@github.com:ianparo/bastion.git\\n\"),\n138\t            Some(\"ianparo/bastion\".into())\n139\t        );\n140\t        assert_eq!(\n141\t            slug_of(\"https://github.com/ianparo/bastion\"),\n142\t            Some(\"ianparo/bastion\".into())\n143\t        );\n144\t        assert_eq!(slug_of(\"git@gitlab.com:o/r.git\"), None);\n145\t        assert_eq!(slug_of(\"/tmp/demo-a\"), None);\n146\t    }\n147\t}\n148\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"3fe8b5c7-b534-47b0-a83b-29a127506743","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-core/src/tests.rs","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-core/src/tests.rs","content":"//! The job state machine on workflows of steps (D39).\n\nuse super::*;\nuse crate::workflow::{Reach, Step};\n\nconst AT: u64 = 1_000;\n\nfn prompt(id: &str, dial: Dial) -> Step {\n    Step {\n        id: id.into(),\n        stage: Stage::Prompt,\n        run: String::new(),\n        dial,\n        note: \"Do it.\".into(),\n        needs: Vec::new(),\n        gives: Vec::new(),\n        reach: Reach::default(),\n    }\n}\n\nfn shell(id: &str, dial: Dial) -> Step {\n    Step {\n        stage: Stage::Shell,\n        run: \"make test\".into(),\n        ..prompt(id, dial)\n    }\n}\n\n/// A running job on plan, build and tests, at its first step.\nfn job(dials: [Dial; 3]) -> Job {\n    let mut plan = prompt(\"plan\", dials[0]);\n    plan.reach.reads_only = true;\n    plan.gives = vec![\"plan\".into()];\n    let mut build = prompt(\"build\", dials[1]);\n    build.needs = vec![\"plan\".into()];\n    let flow = vec![plan, build, shell(\"tests\", dials[2])];\n    let mut j = Job::new(\"j1\".into(), \"w\".into(), \"Add x\".into(), AT).running(flow);\n    j.state = State::Running;\n    j\n}\n\nfn go(j: &Job, e: Event) -> (Job, Vec<Effect>) {\n    step(j, &e, AT + 1, &Bounds::default())\n}\n\nfn done(report: &str) -> Event {\n    Event::TurnFinished {\n        outcome: Outcome::Done {\n            report: report.into(),\n        },\n    }\n}\n\nfn kinds(effects: &[Effect]) -> Vec<&'static str> {\n    effects\n        .iter()\n        .map(|e| match e {\n            Effect::Provision => \"provision\",\n            Effect::StartTurn { .. } => \"turn\",\n            Effect::RecordArtifact { .. } => \"artifact\",\n            Effect::CaptureDiff => \"diff\",\n            Effect::RunStep { .. } => \"run\",\n            Effect::Finish => \"finish\",\n            Effect::Teardown => \"teardown\",\n            Effect::DarkDecided { .. } => \"dark\",\n        })\n        .collect()\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn a_job_runs_its_steps_waits_where_lit_and_finishes_past_the_last() {\n    let j = job([Dial::LightsOn, Dial::Dark, Dial::Dark]);\n    let (j, effects) = go(&j, done(\"RESULT plan:\\n1. Add x.\"));\n    assert_eq!(\n        kinds(&effects),\n        [\"artifact\"],\n        \"a step that only reads leaves no diff\"\n    );\n    assert_eq!(\n        (j.state, j.results[\"plan\"].as_str()),\n        (State::NeedsYou, \"1. Add x.\")\n    );\n    let (j, effects) = go(&j, Event::Approved);\n    assert_eq!(\n        (j.node.as_deref(), kinds(&effects)),\n        (Some(\"build\"), vec![\"turn\"])\n    );\n    let Effect::StartTurn { brief, .. } = &effects[0] else {\n        panic!()\n    };\n    assert!(\n        brief.contains(\"<result name=\\\"plan\\\">\\n1. Add x.\"),\n        \"{brief}\"\n    );\n    let (j, effects) = go(&j, done(\"Built.\"));\n    assert_eq!(kinds(&effects), [\"artifact\", \"diff\", \"dark\", \"run\"]);\n    let (j, effects) = go(\n        &j,\n        Event::Ran {\n            output: \"3 passed\".into(),\n        },\n    );\n    assert_eq!(kinds(&effects), [\"artifact\", \"dark\", \"finish\"]);\n    assert_eq!(\n        (j.state, j.node.as_deref(), j.finishing()),\n        (State::Running, None, true)\n    );\n    let (landed, effects) = go(&j, Event::Landed);\n    assert_eq!(\n        (landed.state, kinds(&effects)),\n        (State::Landed, vec![\"teardown\"])\n    );\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn a_failed_finish_waits_and_an_approve_or_a_restart_finishes_again() {\n    let mut j = job([Dial::Dark; 3]);\n    j.node = None;\n    let (stuck, _) = go(\n        &j,\n        Event::LandFailed {\n            error: \"conflict\".into(),\n        },\n    );\n    assert_eq!(\n        (stuck.state, stuck.error.as_deref()),\n        (State::NeedsYou, Some(\"conflict\"))\n    );\n    let (again, effects) = go(&stuck, Event::Approved);\n    assert_eq!(\n        (again.state, kinds(&effects)),\n        (State::Running, vec![\"finish\"])\n    );\n    assert_eq!(kinds(&restart(&again)), [\"finish\"]);\n    let trial = Bounds {\n        trial: true,\n        ..Bounds::default()\n    };\n    let mut last = job([Dial::Dark; 3]);\n    last.node = Some(\"tests\".into());\n    last.stage = Stage::Shell;\n    let (stopped, _) = step(\n        &last,\n        &Event::Ran {\n            output: \"ok\".into(),\n        },\n        AT,\n        &trial,\n    );\n    assert_eq!(stopped.state, State::Stopped, \"a trial lands nothing\");\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn a_failing_shell_step_goes_back_to_the_step_that_writes_then_waits() {\n    let mut j = job([Dial::Dark; 3]);\n    (j.node, j.stage) = (Some(\"tests\".into()), Stage::Shell);\n    j.results.insert(\"plan\".into(), \"1. Add x.\".into());\n    let (fixing, effects) = go(\n        &j,\n        Event::StepFailed {\n            detail: \"1 failed\".into(),\n        },\n    );\n    assert_eq!(fixing.node.as_deref(), Some(\"build\"), \"plan only reads\");\n    assert_eq!(kinds(&effects), [\"artifact\", \"turn\"]);\n    assert!(fixing.feedback.as_deref().unwrap().contains(\"1 failed\"));\n    let mut again = fixing.clone();\n    (again.node, again.stage) = (Some(\"tests\".into()), Stage::Shell);\n    let (same, _) = go(\n        &again,\n        Event::StepFailed {\n            detail: \"1 failed\".into(),\n        },\n    );\n    assert_eq!(\n        same.state,\n        State::NeedsYou,\n        \"the same failure word for word waits\"\n    );\n    let spent = Bounds {\n        revision_budget: Some(1),\n        ..Bounds::default()\n    };\n    let (budget, _) = step(\n        &again,\n        &Event::StepFailed {\n            detail: \"2 failed\".into(),\n        },\n        AT,\n        &spent,\n    );\n    assert!(\n        budget\n            .error\n            .unwrap()\n            .starts_with(\"The revision budget of 1 is spent.\")\n    );\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn a_note_sends_the_work_back_and_an_answer_goes_to_the_step_that_asked() {\n    let mut j = job([Dial::LightsOn; 3]);\n    (j.node, j.stage, j.state) = (Some(\"tests\".into()), Stage::Shell, State::NeedsYou);\n    j.results.insert(\"plan\".into(), \"1. Add x.\".into());\n    let (back, effects) = go(\n        &j,\n        Event::Commented {\n            text: \"Name it y.\".into(),\n        },\n    );\n    assert_eq!(\n        (back.node.as_deref(), kinds(&effects)),\n        (Some(\"build\"), vec![\"turn\"])\n    );\n    assert_eq!(back.feedback.as_deref(), Some(\"Name it y.\"));\n    let asked = Event::TurnFinished {\n        outcome: Outcome::Asked {\n            question: \"Which file?\".into(),\n        },\n    };\n    let (waits, _) = go(&job([Dial::Dark; 3]), asked);\n    assert_eq!(actions(&waits), [Action::Answer, Action::Stop]);\n    let (answered, _) = go(\n        &waits,\n        Event::Commented {\n            text: \"calc.py\".into(),\n        },\n    );\n    assert_eq!(answered.node.as_deref(), Some(\"plan\"));\n    assert!(answered.feedback.unwrap().contains(\"The answer: calc.py\"));\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn a_reply_without_its_result_gets_one_more_try_then_waits() {\n    let j = job([Dial::Dark; 3]);\n    let (retry, effects) = go(&j, done(\"No plan here.\"));\n    assert_eq!(\n        (retry.state, kinds(&effects)),\n        (State::Running, vec![\"artifact\", \"turn\"])\n    );\n    assert!(retry.feedback.unwrap().contains(\"RESULT plan:\"));\n    let (j, _) = go(&j, done(\"No plan here.\"));\n    let (waits, _) = go(&j, done(\"Still none.\"));\n    assert_eq!(waits.state, State::NeedsYou);\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn a_step_shows_where_it_stands_and_a_queue_admits_by_its_limits() {\n    let mut j = job([Dial::Dark; 3]);\n    j.node = Some(\"build\".into());\n    let shown: Vec<StepState> = steps(&j).into_iter().map(|s| s.2).collect();\n    assert_eq!(\n        shown,\n        [StepState::Done, StepState::Running, StepState::Pending]\n    );\n    let queued = |id: &str, w: &str| Job::new(id.into(), w.into(), \"r\".into(), AT);\n    let jobs = [queued(\"a\", \"w\"), queued(\"b\", \"w\"), queued(\"c\", \"v\")];\n    assert_eq!(admit(&jobs, 2, |w| (w == \"w\").then_some(1)), [\"a\", \"c\"]);\n}\n","numLines":260,"startLine":1,"totalLines":260}},"displayPath":"crates/bastion-core/src/tests.rs"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cf3b8df3-9a0b-4619-b443-bbc3edb8c388","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:30:14.584Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-core/src/tests.rs\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t//! The job state machine on workflows of steps (D39).\n2\t\n3\tuse super::*;\n4\tuse crate::workflow::{Reach, Step};\n5\t\n6\tconst AT: u64 = 1_000;\n7\t\n8\tfn prompt(id: &str, dial: Dial) -> Step {\n9\t    Step {\n10\t        id: id.into(),\n11\t        stage: Stage::Prompt,\n12\t        run: String::new(),\n13\t        dial,\n14\t        note: \"Do it.\".into(),\n15\t        needs: Vec::new(),\n16\t        gives: Vec::new(),\n17\t        reach: Reach::default(),\n18\t    }\n19\t}\n20\t\n21\tfn shell(id: &str, dial: Dial) -> Step {\n22\t    Step {\n23\t        stage: Stage::Shell,\n24\t        run: \"make test\".into(),\n25\t        ..prompt(id, dial)\n26\t    }\n27\t}\n28\t\n29\t/// A running job on plan, build and tests, at its first step.\n30\tfn job(dials: [Dial; 3]) -> Job {\n31\t    let mut plan = prompt(\"plan\", dials[0]);\n32\t    plan.reach.reads_only = true;\n33\t    plan.gives = vec![\"plan\".into()];\n34\t    let mut build = prompt(\"build\", dials[1]);\n35\t    build.needs = vec![\"plan\".into()];\n36\t    let flow = vec![plan, build, shell(\"tests\", dials[2])];\n37\t    let mut j = Job::new(\"j1\".into(), \"w\".into(), \"Add x\".into(), AT).running(flow);\n38\t    j.state = State::Running;\n39\