{"parentUuid":"90a74d6b-bdf6-4d76-a390-447fa26a71b9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwsVmjU6bpKKSx8zdy8X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TJzPEuD41o5kNzuLHkW656","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef edit(p, pairs):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    for a,b in pairs:\n        assert s.count(a)==1,(p,a[:60]); s=s.replace(a,b)\n    open(p,'w').write(s)\nedit('README.md',[('''it through a workflow, and a reviewed change comes out. A workflow is a graph\nof steps (Bastion's own stages, skills, prompts and commands) that you see on\na canvas, and each step waits for your approval or runs on its own, as you set\nit.''','''it through a workflow, and a reviewed change comes out. A workflow is a graph\nof steps that you see on a canvas. Each step is a prompt, an agent, a skill, a\ncommand or a shell script, each with one text you edit, and each waits for\nyour approval or runs on its own, as you set it. Bastion ships the common\nworkflows with their text filled in, and every word of them is yours to\nchange.'''),('''- `gh`, signed in, for pushes and pull requests. Landing locally works\n  without it.''','''- A `GH_TOKEN` in the stack's vault for the workflows that open pull\n  requests: their shell steps ask for the network and that secret. A workflow\n  that merges on this machine works without it.''')])\nedit('DECISIONS.md',[('''| D14 | Every agent turn runs in an `iii-sandbox` VM on its job's worktree. No credential enters the VM; pushes and pull requests happen on the host. |''','''| D14 | Every agent turn runs in an `iii-sandbox` VM on its job's worktree. No credential enters an agent's VM. A shell step that needs one asks for it (D40). |'''),\n('''| D17 | Every job runs a workflow. A free-form task is a short workflow, not a second mode. |''','''| D17 | Every job runs a workflow. A free-form task is the shipped Short workflow, not a second mode. |'''),\n('''| D23 | Forge, tracker, CI, model providers and notifications are adapters behind seams, chosen in Settings. |''','''| D23 | The tracker, model providers and notifications are adapters behind seams, chosen in Settings. Pull requests, CI and merges are a workflow's shell steps (D39). |'''),\n('''| D35 | A workflow is a graph of steps a person edits on a canvas. Steps pass declared results to the steps linked after them. |''','''| D35 | A workflow is a graph of steps a person edits on a canvas. Steps pass declared results to the steps linked after them. |'''),\n('''| D38 | Every client goes through `crates/bastion-client`: the server list, typed calls, and the event stream. A new interface adds pages, not a second way to talk to a server. |''','''| D38 | Every client goes through `crates/bastion-client`: the server list, typed calls, and the event stream. A new interface adds pages, not a second way to talk to a server. |\n| D39 | A workflow is a series of steps, and nothing else runs. A step is a prompt, an agent (`.claude/agents`), a skill (`.claude/skills`), a command (`.claude/commands`) or a shell script, each with one text. Bastion's built-in stages are gone. |\n| D40 | A shell step runs in the job's VM, with no network unless it asks. A step that asks gets a VM of its own with the network and the vault secrets it names as environment variables. |\n| D41 | A job ends with its branch ready. When the last step passes, a workspace set to merge merges the branch into its base on the host; one set to leave keeps the branch. |\n| D42 | Governance is per step. A step may change files or only reads, and the gate refuses a write from a step that only reads. Dials, notices, artifacts and evals name steps. |''')])\ns=open('PLAN.md').read()\na='''- Exit: no `Stage` in the code but the five kinds, and every CI step passes.\n'''\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,a+'''\nDone 2026-11-11. The pipelines, the stage machine, scope splits, discover\nquestions, acceptance tests, UAT sign-off, learn, the presets, the forge\nsetting and the CI and deploy watches are gone. Escapes stay: a revert of\na landed commit still counts against its job. Migration 5 deletes the\nnodes of stages Bastion ran itself, with their links and results, and\nmakes every other stage a prompt; a stage that only read becomes a prompt\nthat only reads. Each artifact now names the step it came from, so the job\npage shows a step's own reports. Live: the dev database moved to version 5\nwith only prompt and shell nodes left, and a Short job ran on\n`demo-local`.\n''')\nopen('PLAN.md','w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"D18\\|stage\" DECISIONS.md | head","description":"Update README, DECISIONS, PLAN for S4"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2896,"cache_read_input_tokens":287935,"output_tokens":1869,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":163},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2896,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1869,"cache_read_input_tokens":287935,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2896,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2896},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TJzPEuD41o5kNzuLHkW656":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef edit(p, pairs):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    for a,b in pairs:\n        assert s.count(a)==1,(p,a[:60]); s=s.replace(a,b)\n    open(p,'w').write(s)\nedit('README.md',[('''it through a workflow, and a reviewed change comes out. A workflow is a graph\nof steps (Bastion's own stages, skills, prompts and commands) that you see on\na canvas, and each step waits for your approval or runs on its own, as you set\nit.''','''it through a workflow, and a reviewed change comes out. A workflow is a graph\nof steps that you see on a canvas. Each step is a prompt, an agent, a skill, a\ncommand or a shell script, each with one text you edit, and each waits for\nyour approval or runs on its own, as you set it. Bastion ships the common\nworkflows with their text filled in, and every word of them is yours to\nchange.'''),('''- `gh`, signed in, for pushes and pull requests. Landing locally works\n  without it.''','''- A `GH_TOKEN` in the stack's vault for the workflows that open pull\n  requests: their shell steps ask for the network and that secret. A workflow\n  that merges on this machine works without it.''')])\nedit('DECISIONS.md',[('''| D14 | Every agent turn runs in an `iii-sandbox` VM on its job's worktree. No credential enters the VM; pushes and pull requests happen on the host. |''','''| D14 | Every agent turn runs in an `iii-sandbox` VM on its job's worktree. No credential enters an agent's VM. A shell step that needs one asks for it (D40). |'''),\n('''| D17 | Every job runs a workflow. A free-form task is a short workflow, not a second mode. |''','''| D17 | Every job runs a workflow. A free-form task is the shipped Short workflow, not a second mode. |'''),\n('''| D23 | Forge, tracker, CI, model providers and notifications are adapters behind seams, chosen in Settings. |''','''| D23 | The tracker, model providers and notifications are adapters behind seams, chosen in Settings. Pull requests, CI and merges are a workflow's shell steps (D39). |'''),\n('''| D35 | A workflow is a graph of steps a person edits on a canvas. Steps pass declared results to the steps linked after them. |''','''| D35 | A workflow is a graph of steps a person edits on a canvas. Steps pass declared results to the steps linked after them. |'''),\n('''| D38 | Every client goes through `crates/bastion-client`: the server list, typed calls, and the event stream. A new interface adds pages, not a second way to talk to a server. |''','''| D38 | Every client goes through `crates/bastion-client`: the server list, typed calls, and the event stream. A new interface adds pages, not a second way to talk to a server. |\n| D39 | A workflow is a series of steps, and nothing else runs. A step is a prompt, an agent (`.claude/agents`), a skill (`.claude/skills`), a command (`.claude/commands`) or a shell script, each with one text. Bastion's built-in stages are gone. |\n| D40 | A shell step runs in the job's VM, with no network unless it asks. A step that asks gets a VM of its own with the network and the vault secrets it names as environment variables. |\n| D41 | A job ends with its branch ready. When the last step passes, a workspace set to merge merges the branch into its base on the host; one set to leave keeps the branch. |\n| D42 | Governance is per step. A step may change files or only reads, and the gate refuses a write from a step that only reads. Dials, notices, artifacts and evals name steps. |''')])\ns=open('PLAN.md').read()\na='''- Exit: no `Stage` in the code but the five kinds, and every CI step passes.\n'''\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,a+'''\nDone 2026-11-11. The pipelines, the stage machine, scope splits, discover\nquestions, acceptance tests, UAT sign-off, learn, the presets, the forge\nsetting and the CI and deploy watches are gone. Escapes stay: a revert of\na landed commit still counts against its job. Migration 5 deletes the\nnodes of stages Bastion ran itself, with their links and results, and\nmakes every other stage a prompt; a stage that only read becomes a prompt\nthat only reads. Each artifact now names the step it came from, so the job\npage shows a step's own reports. Live: the dev database moved to version 5\nwith only prompt and shell nodes left, and a Short job ran on\n`demo-local`.\n''')\nopen('PLAN.md','w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"D18\\|stage\" DECISIONS.md | head","description":"Update README, DECISIONS,