{"parentUuid":"b51c4ca7-e307-4ac7-8a66-7e6fb045cd04","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01TJzPEuD41o5kNzuLHkW656","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"if [ -n \"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR:-}\" ] && [ -x /bin/zsh ]; then exec /bin/zsh -fc 'LC_ALL=C␤export CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-$PPID}␤export CMUX_AGENT_HOOK_INVOKER_PID=$PPID␤cmux_fallback() { { print -rn -- \"$cmux_p\"; /bin/cat; } | /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3; exit $?; }␤zmodload zsh/system zsh/datetime zsh/files 2>/dev/null || exec /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3␤cmux_p= cmux_c= cmux_e=0␤while (( ${#cmux_p} < 262144 )); do sysread -i 0 -s 65536 cmux_c || { cmux_e=$?; break; }; cmux_p+=$cmux_c; done␤[[ -n ${CMUX_SURFACE_ID:-} && ${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED:-} != 1 ]] || { (( cmux_e == 5 )) || /bin/cat >/dev/null; print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3; exit 0; }␤cmux_d=$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR␤(( cmux_e == 5 )) && [[ -f $cmux_d/keys ]] || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤cmux_r=\"cmux-agent-hook-v1\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"claude\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"$2\"$'\\''\\n'\\''␤for cmux_k in ${(f)\"$(<$cmux_d/keys)\"}; do (( ${+parameters[$cmux_k]} )) && cmux_r+=\"$cmux_k=${(P)cmux_k}\"$'\\''\\0'\\''; done␤cmux_r+=$'\\''\\0'\\''\"$cmux_p\"␤(( ${#cmux_r} <= 524288 )) || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤umask 077␤cmux_n=$cmux_d/$epochtime[1].$epochtime[2]-$$␤{ print -rn -- \"$cmux_r\" >| $cmux_n.tmp && mv -f -- $cmux_n.tmp $cmux_n.rec; } 2>/dev/null || { rm -f -- $cmux_n.tmp 2>/dev/null; cmux_fallback \"$1\"; }␤if zsystem flock -t 0 -r -f cmux_l $cmux_d/forwarder.lock 2>/dev/null; then␤  zsystem flock -u $cmux_l␤  rm -- $cmux_n.rec 2>/dev/null && cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤fi␤print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3' cmux-hook 'cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; fi' pre-tool-use 3>&1 1>&2; else cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; fi; fi","durationMs":41},"type":"attachment","uuid":"16e46ae5-8f6c-4941-aadb-476c83263820","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:44:24.023Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"b51c4ca7-e307-4ac7-8a66-7e6fb045cd04","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1d9ef2db-03d5-4a58-b720-e211c5a548e5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TJzPEuD41o5kNzuLHkW656","type":"tool_result","content":"45:| D18 | The factory's rules live in `bastion-core`: pure functions from an event and a state to a new state and effects, with no I/O and no `async`. |\n65:| D39 | A workflow is a series of steps, and nothing else runs. A step is a prompt, an agent (`.claude/agents`), a skill (`.claude/skills`), a command (`.claude/commands`) or a shell script, each with one text. Bastion's built-in stages are gone. |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a6e29855-70a1-4feb-a138-989af54671ea","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:44:24.299Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"45:| D18 | The factory's rules live in `bastion-core`: pure functions from an event and a state to a new state and effects, with no I/O and no `async`. |\n65:| D39 | A workflow is a series of steps, and nothing else runs. A step is a prompt, an agent (`.claude/agents`), a skill (`.claude/skills`), a command (`.claude/commands`) or a shell script, each with one text. Bastion's built-in stages are gone. |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":39,"oldLines":15,"newStart":39,"newLines":15,"lines":[" | D8 | Records live in the `database` worker as typed columns. Each row carries a `rev`, and a stale write is refused. |"," | D10 | Updates are pushed, never polled: the server observes the engine, and clients follow the server's events (D29). |"," | D13 | The local server starts the stack (`iii compose`) and attaches to one that already runs. The stack goes down when the server stops. A client attaches to the local server or starts it, and quitting a client leaves both running. |","-| D14 | Every agent turn runs in an `iii-sandbox` VM on its job's worktree. No credential enters the VM; pushes and pull requests happen on the host. |","+| D14 | Every agent turn runs in an `iii-sandbox` VM on its job's worktree. No credential enters an agent's VM. A shell step that needs one asks for it (D40). |"," | D16 | A note on a step goes to the agent word for word as its next brief. A fix loop stops after a set count, or sooner when a refusal repeats word for word. |","-| D17 | Every job runs a workflow. A free-form task is a short workflow, not a second mode. |","+| D17 | Every job runs a workflow. A free-form task is the shipped Short workflow, not a second mode. |"," | D18 | The factory's rules live in `bastion-core`: pure functions from an event and a state to a new state and effects, with no I/O and no `async`. |"," | D19 | The seams are Cargo dependencies, and `scripts/check-seams.sh` fails CI when one is crossed. Only the engine adapter imports `iii-sdk`. Clients depend on `bastion-protocol` and the client library only. |"," | D20 | Every constraint and capability is enforced in a hook, and its rung is data, so an eval can name what changed. |"," | D21 | The audit record is a hash chain with one writer. Each entry carries an HMAC-SHA256 of its fields and the entry before it, keyed with a secret outside the record. |"," | D22 | An eval compares two harness configurations on the same requests from the same commit, and reports the difference with the decisions behind it. |","-| D23 | Forge, tracker, CI, model providers and notifications are adapters behind seams, chosen in Settings. |","+| D23 | The tracker, model providers and notifications are adapters behind seams, chosen in Settings. Pull requests, CI and merges are a workflow's shell steps (D39). |"," | D25 | Every rule belongs to one layer: the charter (the repository's own), the harness (an agent's calls), or the factory (the workflow). |"," | D26 | Rules, grants and settings are data in the server's database, versioned, edited on the pages; first-run defaults come from `seed/governance.sql`. |"," | D27 | The server is the source of truth and holds all business logic. A client shows state and sends a person's actions, nothing more. |"]},{"oldStart":62,"oldLines":6,"newStart":62,"newLines":10,"lines":[" | D36 | Claude takes an API key only. No Claude subscription sign-in. |"," | D37 | The desktop client is a native Rust app on `iced`. It holds no factory logic and reaches a server only through the client library. |"," | D38 | Every client goes through `crates/bastion-client`: the server list, typed calls, and the event stream. A new interface adds pages, not a second way to talk to a server. |","+| D39 | A workflow is a series of steps, and nothing else runs. A step is a prompt, an agent (`.claude/agents`), a skill (`.claude/skills`), a command (`.claude/commands`) or a shell script, each with one text. Bastion's built-in stages are gone. |","+| D40 | A shell step runs in the job's VM, with no network unless it asks. A step that asks gets a VM of its own with the network and the vault secrets it names as environment variables. |","+| D41 | A job ends with its branch ready. When the last step passes, a workspace set to merge merges the branch into its base on the host; one set to leave keeps the branch. |","+| D42 | Governance is per step. A step may change files or only reads, and the gate refuses a write from a step that only reads. Dials, notices, artifacts and evals name steps. |"," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":107,"oldLines":6,"newStart":107,"newLines":17,"lines":["   Bastion is now."," - Exit: no `Stage` in the code but the five kinds, and every CI step passes."," ","+Done 2026-11-11. The pipelines, the stage machine, scope splits, discover","+questions, acceptance tests, UAT sign-off, learn, the presets, the forge","+setting and the CI and deploy watches are gone. Escapes stay: a revert of","+a landed commit still counts against its job. Migration 5 deletes the","+nodes of stages Bastion ran itself, with their links and results, and","+makes every other stage a prompt; a stage that only read becomes a prompt","+that only reads. Each artifact now names the step it came from, so the job","+page shows a step's own reports. Live: the dev database moved to version 5","+with only prompt and shell nodes left, and a Short job ran on","+`demo-local`.","+"," ## Open questions"," "," - **What learn and escapes become.** Both read a landed job's history. They"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":9,"newStart":2,"newLines":11,"lines":[" "," Bastion is a software factory you can govern. A request goes in, agents work"," it through a workflow, and a reviewed change comes out. A workflow is a graph","-of steps (Bastion's own stages, skills, prompts and commands) that you see on","-a canvas, and each step waits for your approval or runs on its own, as you set","-it. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server` runs the factory on","+of steps that you see on a canvas. Each step is a prompt, an agent, a skill, a","+command or a shell script, each with one text you edit, and each waits for","+your approval or runs on its own, as you set it. Bastion ships the common","+workflows with their text filled in, and every word of them is yours to","+change. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server` runs the factory on"," the [iii](https://iii.dev) engine, and the desktop app (on"," [iced](https://iced.rs)) and the `bastion` command line talk to it over HTTP."," It's early. [VISION.md](VISION.md) says where it is going, and"]},{"oldStart":49,"oldLines":8,"newStart":51,"newLines":9,"lines":[" - `iii` 0.25.0 on your `PATH`."," - A model provider key, set in **Settings**, which keeps it in the stack's","   vault. A key in the environment works too.","-- `gh`, signed in, for pushes and pull requests. Landing locally works","-  without it.","+- A `GH_TOKEN` in the stack's vault for the workflows that open pull","+  requests: their shell steps ask for the network and that secret. A workflow","+  that merges on this machine works without it."," "," If something is missing, Doctor on the Engine page names it and says how to"," fix it. A failed required check stops the start."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/README.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a9e42607-f26f-4643-b741-2143db11478f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":11,"modified":54,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":3},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b51c4ca7-e307-4ac7-8a66-7e6fb045cd04","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"a6e29855-70a1-4feb-a138-989af54671ea","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","snippet":""},"type":"attachment","uuid":"814fc479-a4ce-4b85-afc1-dd7719fce70f","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:44:24.315Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. The changes are not shown here; use Read if you need the current content.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"814fc479-a4ce-4b85-afc1-dd7719fce70f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/README.md","snippet":"1\t# Bastion\n2\t\n3\tBastion is a software factory you can govern. A request goes in, agents work\n4\tit through a workflow, and a reviewed change comes out. A workflow is a graph\n5\tof steps that you see on a canvas. Each step is a prompt, an agent, a skill, a\n6\tcommand or a shell script, each with one text you edit, and each waits for\n7\tyour approval or runs on its own, as you set it. Bastion ships the common\n8\tworkflows with their text filled in, and every word of them is yours to\n9\tchange. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server` runs the factory on\n10\tthe [iii](https://iii.dev) engine, and the desktop app (on\n11\t[iced](https://iced.rs)) and the `bastion` command line talk to it over HTTP.\n12\tIt's early. [VISION.md](VISION.md) says where it is going, and\n13\t[DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) holds the goals and the decisions behind it.\n14\t\n15\t## Install\n16\t\n17\tOn an Apple Silicon Mac or on Linux, install the server and the CLI, and add\n...\n44\tserver issued them.\n45\t\n46\t## What you need\n47\t\n48\t- Rust, from `rust-toolchain.toml` (rustup picks it up).\n49\t- `iii` 0.25.0 on your `PATH`.\n50\t- A model provider key, set in **Settings**, which keeps it in the stack's\n51\t  vault. A key in the environment works too.\n52\t- A `GH_TOKEN` in the stack's vault for the workflows that open pull\n53\t  requests: their shell steps ask for the network and that secret. A workflow\n54\t  that merges on this machine works without it.\n55\t\n56\tIf something is missing, Doctor on the Engine page names it and says how to\n57\tfix it. A failed required check stops the start.\n58\t\n59\t## How it fits together\n60\t\n61\t| Part | Where | Does |\n62\t|---|---|---|"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e62ac3b2-258f-4c0b-8ff8-643d6ef44458","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:44:24.315Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/README.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n1\t# Bastion\n2\t\n3\tBastion is a software factory you can govern. A request goes in, agents work\n4\tit through a workflow, and a reviewed change comes out. A workflow is a graph\n5\tof steps that you see on a canvas. Each step is a prompt, an agent, a skill, a\n6\tcommand or a shell script, each with one text you edit, and each waits for\n7\tyour approval or runs on its own, as you set it. Bastion ships the common\n8\tworkflows with their text filled in, and every word of them is yours to\n9\tchange. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server` runs the factory on\n10\tthe [iii](https://iii.dev) engine, and the desktop app (on\n11\t[iced](https://iced.rs)) and the `bastion` command line talk to it over HTTP.\n12\tIt's early. [VISION.md](VISION.md) says where it is going, and\n13\t[DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) holds the goals and the decisions behind it.\n14\t\n15\t## Install\n16\t\n17\tOn an Apple Silicon Mac or on Linux, install the server and the CLI, and add\n...\n44\tserver issued them.\n45\t\n46\t## What you need\n47\t\n48\t- Rust, from `rust-toolchain.toml` (rustup picks it up).\n49\t- `iii` 0.25.0 on your `PATH`.\n50\t- A model provider key, set in **Settings**, which keeps it in the stack's\n51\t  vault. A key in the environment works too.\n52\t- A `GH_TOKEN` in the stack's vault for the workflows that open pull\n53\t  requests: their shell steps ask for the network and that secret. A workflow\n54\t  that merges on this machine works without it.\n55\t\n56\tIf something is missing, Doctor on the Engine page names it and says how to\n57\tfix it. A failed required check stops the start.\n58\t\n59\t## How it fits together\n60\t\n61\t| Part | Where | Does |\n62\t|---|---|---|\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
