{"parentUuid":"a1a4f848-6bb0-46ed-a6da-76fc11ff4eb6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwsiebDPXNc2bTUBjKfD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"S4 is committed as `8134add`, on top of `bbddad0` (the learn removal). Neither commit is pushed.\n\n**S4 result**\n- Only the five step kinds remain: prompt, agent, skill, command, shell. The pipelines, scope splits, acceptance tests, UAT sign-off, presets, the forge setting, and the CI and deploy watches are gone.\n- Escapes stay. A revert of a landed commit still counts against its job.\n- Each artifact now records the step it came from, and a turn's session is named by its step. Before this, two prompt steps in one workflow would share reports and replies.\n- Migration 5 ran on the dev DB. It is now at version 5 with only prompt and shell nodes. I backed up the DB first to `scratchpad/bastion-before-s4.db`.\n- Live: a Short job landed `triple(x)` on `demo-local`. I approved its two waits, at plan and at checks.\n- The live run found two bugs, now fixed:\n  - The build's diff took the next step's kind.\n  - \"Reset to the original\" deleted a shipped workflow, and it did not come back until a restart.\n- The dev DB's Short was saved in S2, before plan became read-only, so its plan could write. I reset it through the API, and Short v3 has a read-only plan.\n- All four CI steps pass (`fmt --check`, seams, clippy `-D warnings`, `test --workspace`), and the CodeScene safeguard passes. CodeScene suggests adding its instructions to CLAUDE.md. The repo's CLAUDE.md already has the same rule, so I did not change it.\n- DECISIONS.md has D39 to D42, with D14, D17 and D23 updated. The README describes steps, and PLAN.md records S4.\n\n**Hosting plans**\n\n`docs/hosting/hetzner.md` and `docs/hosting/digitalocean.md` are written but not committed. Neither plan was run end to end.\n- **Hetzner:** a Cloud VPS cannot run the sandbox, because Hetzner offers no nested KVM. The plan recommends an AX41 dedicated server at €59 a month, which is sold only in Germany and Finland.\n- **DigitalOcean:** nested KVM is not officially supported. The plan uses a `g-4vcpu-16gb` Droplet at $126 a month and stops after a 1-hour `/dev/kvm` test if KVM is missing.\n- **Both:** only ports 22 and 443 are open. Caddy terminates TLS, so the server stays on loopback and a certificate renewal doesn't restart it.\n- **Code gaps that both plans found:**\n  - `bastion update` keeps the old systemd unit and its versioned `data/` folder.\n  - The app has no way to put `GH_TOKEN` into the vault.\n  - The service's `PATH` doesn't include `iii`.\n\n**Your new requests, queued in this order:**\n1. A top bar with the castle image, replacing the sidebar. This one is next.\n2. An all-servers view for the audit log and costs pages, like the jobs pages.\n3. A model choice on each step.\n4. A workflow that looks like a flowchart, with branches. Today a failure only waits for you or goes back to the step that writes. Your request means a workflow could also have a failure edge to another step. That changes the core state machine, so I'll write it as a decision in PLAN.md before I build it.\n\nShould I push S4 and commit the hosting docs?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":449,"cache_read_input_tokens":305409,"output_tokens":1526,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":383},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":449,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1526,"cache_read_input_tokens":305409,"cache_creation_input_tokens":449,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":449},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7a32644e-d24a-46a0-8eb9-24a68f5d551d","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwsieD8sA4vBjFEqCbCB","type":"assistant","uuid":"5a6f466c-0476-43af-9254-bb767fdd2291","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:47:18.051Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
