{"parentUuid":"c8d82bc0-7878-455d-ac7d-b4002b98a21c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_additional_context","content":["CAVEMAN MODE ACTIVE (caveman). Respond terse like smart caveman. All technical substance stay. Only fluff die. Answer only what was asked: no unrequested background, lists, examples, walkthroughs, or follow-up offers; give code, steps, or warnings when the task needs them. Security warnings, irreversible actions, multi-step order: normal prose. Technical terms, code, commands, paths, and errors stay exact."],"hookName":"UserPromptSubmit","toolUseID":"hook-d95eeff6-40ff-478c-a4e1-bbdef5d86972","hookEvent":"UserPromptSubmit"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e1e8a1f2-8fe4-4bdf-8afd-9de94a8320eb","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:47:23.367Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nUserPromptSubmit hook additional context: CAVEMAN MODE ACTIVE (caveman). Respond terse like smart caveman. All technical substance stay. Only fluff die. Answer only what was asked: no unrequested background, lists, examples, walkthroughs, or follow-up offers; give code, steps, or warnings when the task needs them. Security warnings, irreversible actions, multi-step order: normal prose. Technical terms, code, commands, paths, and errors stay exact.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"e1e8a1f2-8fe4-4bdf-8afd-9de94a8320eb","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"instructions","files":[{"path":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/CLAUDE.md","type":"Project","content":"# CLAUDE.md\n\n## The project\n\nBastion is a server and its clients. [VISION.md](VISION.md) says what the\nproduct is for and how its pages split between jobs and servers.\n[DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) holds the\ngoals and the decisions (cited in code as `DECISIONS.md D<n>`); read it\nbefore a change.\n\n- `crates/bastion-core`: the factory's rules, pure. It may depend only on\n  `serde` and `sha2`.\n- `crates/bastion-protocol`: the API's types and routes. Only `serde`.\n- `crates/bastion-server`: the HTTP API, events, the factory adapter, the\n  store, the gate, the audit, the stack. Only `src/engine/` imports `iii-sdk`.\n- `crates/bastion-client`: what every interface uses to reach a server: the\n  server list, the local server's start, the API calls, the event stream.\n  Never `bastion-core` or `iii-sdk`.\n- `crates/bastion-cli`: the `bastion` command line, on `bastion-client`.\n- `crates/bastion-desktop`: the iced client. It reaches a server only through\n  `bastion-client`; never through `bastion-core` or `iii-sdk`.\n- `workers/`: Bastion's own iii workers.\n\n## Before a commit\n\nRun `pre_commit_code_health_safeguard` and commit only when it passes. After\nchanging code, run `code_health_review` on the changed files, and if Code\nHealth drops, fix it and confirm with `code_health_score`.\n\n## Before a push\n\nRun every CI step, not only the tests:\n\n```sh\ncargo fmt --all -- --check\nscripts/check-seams.sh\ncargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings\ncargo test --workspace\n```"},{"path":"/Users/tacoda/.claude/projects/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/memory/MEMORY.md","type":"AutoMem","content":"# Memory index\n\n- [Bastion dev workflow](bastion-dev-workflow.md) — phase-by-phase, browser-verified loop; frontend runs locally, backend in Docker\n- [Bastion deploy](bastion-deploy.md) — Heroku app DESTROYED 2026-07-16; single-role RLS + PG/Redis TLS gotchas kept for redeploy\n- [Bastion governance package](bastion-governance-package.md) — sibling repo ~/tacoda/tacoda/bastion-governance; @bastion/governance npm CLI+SDK; control plane governs not invokes\n- [Prefer momentum over asking](prefer-momentum-over-asking.md) — proceed on stated assumptions; reserve questions for costly forks; keep current Policy model\n- [Push over pull](push-over-pull.md) — iii.observe over polling triggers (Bastion F25)\n- [Bastion Rust app](bastion-rust-app.md) — native Rust factory on iii, job-first UI like GitHub Actions, wipp pipeline, no editor; DECISIONS.md holds the decisions\n- [Bastion server terminology](bastion-server-terminology.md) — say \"Bastion server\", never target/profile; servers hold workspaces (one per repo); job picks server\n- [Multi-user and hosting are open](bastion-multi-user-hosting-open.md) — open questions in DECISIONS.md, not non-goals; never claim \"not hosted\" or \"one owner\"\n- [Local needs no credentials](bastion-local-needs-no-credentials.md) — local Bastion server: automatic token only; tokens and people are for remote servers\n- [Run every CI step](bastion-run-every-ci-step.md) — seams and -D warnings clippy before each push; core may not use serde_json\n- [Factory, not orchestrator](bastion-orchestrator-terminology.md) — rebrand to orchestrator/control plane rolled back 2026-11-06; keep factory words\n- [No full process args](no-full-process-args.md) — never pgrep -fl/ps aux; iii VM boot lines carry host secrets\n- [Only Dark runs unsupervised](only-dark-runs-unsupervised.md) — lights-on waits for a person; Claude may act for the user on test jobs, saying each action"}],"changed":true,"reason":"compaction"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"84b44e64-510f-4a0c-8c45-aa1ef683d304","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:47:23.385Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nInstruction files were re-read after the conversation was compacted; these differ from their earlier copies — each replaces its earlier copy, and the instructions preamble above still applies:\n\nContents of /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/CLAUDE.md (project instructions, checked into the codebase):\n\n# CLAUDE.md\n\n## The project\n\nBastion is a server and its clients. [VISION.md](VISION.md) says what the\nproduct is for and how its pages split between jobs and servers.\n[DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) holds the\ngoals and the decisions (cited in code as `DECISIONS.md D<n>`); read it\nbefore a change.\n\n- `crates/bastion-core`: the factory's rules, pure. It may depend only on\n  `serde` and `sha2`.\n- `crates/bastion-protocol`: the API's types and routes. Only `serde`.\n- `crates/bastion-server`: the HTTP API, events, the factory adapter, the\n  store, the gate, the audit, the stack. Only `src/engine/` imports `iii-sdk`.\n- `crates/bastion-client`: what every interface uses to reach a server: the\n  server list, the local server's start, the API calls, the event stream.\n  Never `bastion-core` or `iii-sdk`.\n- `crates/bastion-cli`: the `bastion` command line, on `bastion-client`.\n- `crates/bastion-desktop`: the iced client. It reaches a server only through\n  `bastion-client`; never through `bastion-core` or `iii-sdk`.\n- `workers/`: Bastion's own iii workers.\n\n## Before a commit\n\nRun `pre_commit_code_health_safeguard` and commit only when it passes. After\nchanging code, run `code_health_review` on the changed files, and if Code\nHealth drops, fix it and confirm with `code_health_score`.\n\n## Before a push\n\nRun every CI step, not only the tests:\n\n```sh\ncargo fmt --all -- --check\nscripts/check-seams.sh\ncargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings\ncargo test --workspace\n```\n\nContents of /Users/tacoda/.claude/projects/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/memory/MEMORY.md (user's auto-memory, persists across conversations):\n\n# Memory index\n\n- [Bastion dev workflow](bastion-dev-workflow.md) — phase-by-phase, browser-verified loop; frontend runs locally, backend in Docker\n- [Bastion deploy](bastion-deploy.md) — Heroku app DESTROYED 2026-07-16; single-role RLS + PG/Redis TLS gotchas kept for redeploy\n- [Bastion governance package](bastion-governance-package.md) — sibling repo ~/tacoda/tacoda/bastion-governance; @bastion/governance npm CLI+SDK; control plane governs not invokes\n- [Prefer momentum over asking](prefer-momentum-over-asking.md) — proceed on stated assumptions; reserve questions for costly forks; keep current Policy model\n- [Push over pull](push-over-pull.md) — iii.observe over polling triggers (Bastion F25)\n- [Bastion Rust app](bastion-rust-app.md) — native Rust factory on iii, job-first UI like GitHub Actions, wipp pipeline, no editor; DECISIONS.md holds the decisions\n- [Bastion server terminology](bastion-server-terminology.md) — say \"Bastion server\", never target/profile; servers hold workspaces (one per repo); job picks server\n- [Multi-user and hosting are open](bastion-multi-user-hosting-open.md) — open questions in DECISIONS.md, not non-goals; never claim \"not hosted\" or \"one owner\"\n- [Local needs no credentials](bastion-local-needs-no-credentials.md) — local Bastion server: automatic token only; tokens and people are for remote servers\n- [Run every CI step](bastion-run-every-ci-step.md) — seams and -D warnings clippy before each push; core may not use serde_json\n- [Factory, not orchestrator](bastion-orchestrator-terminology.md) — rebrand to orchestrator/control plane rolled back 2026-11-06; keep factory words\n- [No full process args](no-full-process-args.md) — never pgrep -fl/ps aux; iii VM boot lines carry host secrets\n- [Only Dark runs unsupervised](only-dark-runs-unsupervised.md) — lights-on waits for a person; Claude may act for the user on test jobs, saying each action\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
