{"parentUuid":"a709891f-5df9-413c-962f-ea5cdc01098e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01T6iRP3RowVydeyu7CeuNfz","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"if [ -n \"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR:-}\" ] && [ -x /bin/zsh ]; then exec /bin/zsh -fc 'LC_ALL=C␤export CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-$PPID}␤export CMUX_AGENT_HOOK_INVOKER_PID=$PPID␤cmux_fallback() { { print -rn -- \"$cmux_p\"; /bin/cat; } | /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3; exit $?; }␤zmodload zsh/system zsh/datetime zsh/files 2>/dev/null || exec /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3␤cmux_p= cmux_c= cmux_e=0␤while (( ${#cmux_p} < 262144 )); do sysread -i 0 -s 65536 cmux_c || { cmux_e=$?; break; }; cmux_p+=$cmux_c; done␤[[ -n ${CMUX_SURFACE_ID:-} && ${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED:-} != 1 ]] || { (( cmux_e == 5 )) || /bin/cat >/dev/null; print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3; exit 0; }␤cmux_d=$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR␤(( cmux_e == 5 )) && [[ -f $cmux_d/keys ]] || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤cmux_r=\"cmux-agent-hook-v1\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"claude\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"$2\"$'\\''\\n'\\''␤for cmux_k in ${(f)\"$(<$cmux_d/keys)\"}; do (( ${+parameters[$cmux_k]} )) && cmux_r+=\"$cmux_k=${(P)cmux_k}\"$'\\''\\0'\\''; done␤cmux_r+=$'\\''\\0'\\''\"$cmux_p\"␤(( ${#cmux_r} <= 524288 )) || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤umask 077␤cmux_n=$cmux_d/$epochtime[1].$epochtime[2]-$$␤{ print -rn -- \"$cmux_r\" >| $cmux_n.tmp && mv -f -- $cmux_n.tmp $cmux_n.rec; } 2>/dev/null || { rm -f -- $cmux_n.tmp 2>/dev/null; cmux_fallback \"$1\"; }␤if zsystem flock -t 0 -r -f cmux_l $cmux_d/forwarder.lock 2>/dev/null; then␤  zsystem flock -u $cmux_l␤  rm -- $cmux_n.rec 2>/dev/null && cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤fi␤print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3' cmux-hook 'cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; fi' pre-tool-use 3>&1 1>&2; else cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; fi; fi","durationMs":54},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b1d0774d-8af0-4ebd-bc67-d721875236e8","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:49:35.451Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"a709891f-5df9-413c-962f-ea5cdc01098e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"386a1d2e-a433-4eb9-8340-e8d4f63e7469","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T6iRP3RowVydeyu7CeuNfz","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# Bastion's vision\n2:\n3:<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n4:\n5:Bastion is a desktop app a developer uses to run jobs through software\n6:factories. A factory is a Bastion server, on your machine or a remote one,\n7:and you can use several at once. You define what each factory does: its\n8:workflows, the capabilities its agents get, and the constraints they work\n9:under. Bastion seeds the common workflows with their text filled in, and\n10:you can change every step of them. The cost is honest: a factory does only\n11:what its workflows say, so a gate you remove is gone.\n12:\n13:## Two levels: your jobs, and each server\n14:\n15:The app has two levels, and every page sits on one of them.\n16:\n17:**Your jobs, across servers.** The Jobs pages list every job on every\n18:server you added, side by side. You filter them by server and by\n19:workspace, open one, and act on it wherever it runs. These pages stay as\n20:they are.\n21:\n22:**One server at a time.** Every other page belongs to the server you pick\n23:at the top: Workflows, Constraints, Capabilities, Audit Log, Evals, Costs,\n24:Verification, Engine and Settings. A page never mixes two\n25:servers, because each server has its own rules and its own records.\n26:\n27:## What a server holds\n28:\n29:A server is a factory, and everything that shapes it lives with it.\n30:\n31:- **Workspaces:** the repositories it works in, each with its checks, its\n32:  setup, its VM image, and what happens to a job's branch at the end.\n33:- **Workflows:** series of steps. A step is a prompt, one of the\n34:  repository's agents, skills or commands, or a shell script. Each step has\n35:  one text to edit, a dial (a sun when a person decides, a moon when it runs\n36:  on its own), and the results it passes on.\n37:- **Capabilities and constraints:** what an agent may call, and the rules\n38:  its work must keep, each on a ladder from told to enforced.\n39:- **Settings:** its model providers, its people and their roles, its\n40:  notifications, and its secrets.\n41:- **Records:** its audit log, its evals, its costs, and what landed.\n42:\n43:These are live controls, not a configuration file you edit and restart.\n44:A server runs on the iii engine, and each value you change in the app\n45:changes how that engine works for the next call or the next job: which\n46:model a turn runs on, which calls an agent may make, which image a VM\n47:boots, what a step does. Bastion's job is to turn the values you set into\n48:how iii behaves.\n49:\n50:The app itself keeps one thing: the list of servers you added. That list\n51:is the only setting that belongs to you and not to a server.\n52:\n53:## Local and remote\n54:\n55:A local server starts with the app and needs no credentials. A remote\n56:server needs a token the server issued you, over TLS. Either kind runs the\n57:same factory, so a workflow written on one works on the other. A job runs\n58:on one server; your jobs can run on many.\n59:\n60:## What does not change\n61:\n62:- Agent code runs in a VM, never on your machine. A step reaches the\n63:  network only when its workflow says so, with the secrets it names.\n64:- Every action names who took it, in the server's audit log.\n65:- A seeded default is a starting point, never a lock.\n66:\n67:## Not this\n68:\n69:Not an editor: the only code you read in Bastion is the change a job\n70:proposes. Not a web app. Not a hosted service, for now.\n71:\n72:## Next\n73:\n74:Go page by page, on the server level first: each page shows the server it\n75:belongs to, and its settings move with that server.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"999d604e-c318-48a1-b315-94f56df452d1","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:49:35.621Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1:# Bastion's vision\n2:\n3:<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n4:\n5:Bastion is a desktop app a developer uses to run jobs through software\n6:factories. A factory is a Bastion server, on your machine or a remote one,\n7:and you can use several at once. You define what each factory does: its\n8:workflows, the capabilities its agents get, and the constraints they work\n9:under. Bastion seeds the common workflows with their text filled in, and\n10:you can change every step of them. The cost is honest: a factory does only\n11:what its workflows say, so a gate you remove is gone.\n12:\n13:## Two levels: your jobs, and each server\n14:\n15:The app has two levels, and every page sits on one of them.\n16:\n17:**Your jobs, across servers.** The Jobs pages list every job on every\n18:server you added, side by side. You filter them by server and by\n19:workspace, open one, and act on it wherever it runs. These pages stay as\n20:they are.\n21:\n22:**One server at a time.** Every other page belongs to the server you pick\n23:at the top: Workflows, Constraints, Capabilities, Audit Log, Evals, Costs,\n24:Verification, Engine and Settings. A page never mixes two\n25:servers, because each server has its own rules and its own records.\n26:\n27:## What a server holds\n28:\n29:A server is a factory, and everything that shapes it lives with it.\n30:\n31:- **Workspaces:** the repositories it works in, each with its checks, its\n32:  setup, its VM image, and what happens to a job's branch at the end.\n33:- **Workflows:** series of steps. A step is a prompt, one of the\n34:  repository's agents, skills or commands, or a shell script. Each step has\n35:  one text to edit, a dial (a sun when a person decides, a moon when it runs\n36:  on its own), and the results it passes on.\n37:- **Capabilities and constraints:** what an agent may call, and the rules\n38:  its work must keep, each on a ladder from told to enforced.\n39:- **Settings:** its model providers, its people and their roles, its\n40:  notifications, and its secrets.\n41:- **Records:** its audit log, its evals, its costs, and what landed.\n42:\n43:These are live controls, not a configuration file you edit and restart.\n44:A server runs on the iii engine, and each value you change in the app\n45:changes how that engine works for the next call or the next job: which\n46:model a turn runs on, which calls an agent may make, which image a VM\n47:boots, what a step does. Bastion's job is to turn the values you set into\n48:how iii behaves.\n49:\n50:The app itself keeps one thing: the list of servers you added. That list\n51:is the only setting that belongs to you and not to a server.\n52:\n53:## Local and remote\n54:\n55:A local server starts with the app and needs no credentials. A remote\n56:server needs a token the server issued you, over TLS. Either kind runs the\n57:same factory, so a workflow written on one works on the other. A job runs\n58:on one server; your jobs can run on many.\n59:\n60:## What does not change\n61:\n62:- Agent code runs in a VM, never on your machine. A step reaches the\n63:  network only when its workflow says so, with the secrets it names.\n64:- Every action names who took it, in the server's audit log.\n65:- A seeded default is a starting point, never a lock.\n66:\n67:## Not this\n68:\n69:Not an editor: the only code you read in Bastion is the change a job\n70:proposes. Not a web app. Not a hosted service, for now.\n71:\n72:## Next\n73:\n74:Go page by page, on the server level first: each page shows the server it\n75:belongs to, and its settings move with that server.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ecadfebb-a3a3-433f-84c5-1cbdccfd4bfa","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a709891f-5df9-413c-962f-ea5cdc01098e","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
