{"parentUuid":"f774c0cd-e9b2-4a08-9ee0-82f9a7d4430a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01FFnmM3zrEURFYe2mkfeZpd","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"if [ -n \"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR:-}\" ] && [ -x /bin/zsh ]; then exec /bin/zsh -fc 'LC_ALL=C␤export CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-$PPID}␤export CMUX_AGENT_HOOK_INVOKER_PID=$PPID␤cmux_fallback() { { print -rn -- \"$cmux_p\"; /bin/cat; } | /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3; exit $?; }␤zmodload zsh/system zsh/datetime zsh/files 2>/dev/null || exec /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3␤cmux_p= cmux_c= cmux_e=0␤while (( ${#cmux_p} < 262144 )); do sysread -i 0 -s 65536 cmux_c || { cmux_e=$?; break; }; cmux_p+=$cmux_c; done␤[[ -n ${CMUX_SURFACE_ID:-} && ${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED:-} != 1 ]] || { (( cmux_e == 5 )) || /bin/cat >/dev/null; print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3; exit 0; }␤cmux_d=$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR␤(( cmux_e == 5 )) && [[ -f $cmux_d/keys ]] || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤cmux_r=\"cmux-agent-hook-v1\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"claude\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"$2\"$'\\''\\n'\\''␤for cmux_k in ${(f)\"$(<$cmux_d/keys)\"}; do (( ${+parameters[$cmux_k]} )) && cmux_r+=\"$cmux_k=${(P)cmux_k}\"$'\\''\\0'\\''; done␤cmux_r+=$'\\''\\0'\\''\"$cmux_p\"␤(( ${#cmux_r} <= 524288 )) || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤umask 077␤cmux_n=$cmux_d/$epochtime[1].$epochtime[2]-$$␤{ print -rn -- \"$cmux_r\" >| $cmux_n.tmp && mv -f -- $cmux_n.tmp $cmux_n.rec; } 2>/dev/null || { rm -f -- $cmux_n.tmp 2>/dev/null; cmux_fallback \"$1\"; }␤if zsystem flock -t 0 -r -f cmux_l $cmux_d/forwarder.lock 2>/dev/null; then␤  zsystem flock -u $cmux_l␤  rm -- $cmux_n.rec 2>/dev/null && cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤fi␤print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3' cmux-hook 'cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; fi' pre-tool-use 3>&1 1>&2; else cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; fi; fi","durationMs":57},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5efacc67-233d-4215-a18c-3e42f728a8ce","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:49:42.822Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"f774c0cd-e9b2-4a08-9ee0-82f9a7d4430a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"386a1d2e-a433-4eb9-8340-e8d4f63e7469","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FFnmM3zrEURFYe2mkfeZpd","type":"tool_result","content":"VISION [informational]  (636 words, 2 findings)\n  - tic not_a_opener: 2 (budget 1) [advisory: a parallel non-goals list is stated scope, not a tic]\n  - first person low for informational register: 0.0/1k words (min 0.5); a standard still needs one or two asides only I can give: why this threshold, what broke first, when I bend it\n\n2 findings across 1 page(s)\nchain: voicecheck -> /humanizer (tone) -> /slopbeth (slop) -> voicecheck (gate)\nno later stage may reintroduce a finding above\nin_progress\t\tHosting plans for a Bastion server on Hetzner and DigitalOcean\tci\tmain\tpush\t43106442585\t10s\t2026-11-11T21:49:33Z\ncompleted\tsuccess\tThe vision: a server's settings are live controls over how iii behaves\tci\tmain\tpush\t43100371653\t1m33s\t2026-11-11T21:07:33Z","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b56c5cb5-f9b7-48fb-9077-32226e240074","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:49:43.949Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"VISION [informational]  (636 words, 2 findings)\n  - tic not_a_opener: 2 (budget 1) [advisory: a parallel non-goals list is stated scope, not a tic]\n  - first person low for informational register: 0.0/1k words (min 0.5); a standard still needs one or two asides only I can give: why this threshold, what broke first, when I bend it\n\n2 findings across 1 page(s)\nchain: voicecheck -> /humanizer (tone) -> /slopbeth (slop) -> voicecheck (gate)\nno later stage may reintroduce a finding above\nin_progress\t\tHosting plans for a Bastion server on Hetzner and DigitalOcean\tci\tmain\tpush\t43106442585\t10s\t2026-11-11T21:49:33Z\ncompleted\tsuccess\tThe vision: a server's settings are live controls over how iii behaves\tci\tmain\tpush\t43100371653\t1m33s\t2026-11-11T21:07:33Z","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/VISION.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":10,"oldLines":19,"newStart":10,"newLines":21,"lines":[" you can change every step of them. The cost is honest: a factory does only"," what its workflows say, so a gate you remove is gone."," ","-## Two levels: your jobs, and each server","+## Two levels: each server, and all of them"," ","-The app has two levels, and every page sits on one of them.","+Every page shows one server, the one you pick at the top. Some pages can","+also show every server at once, and those are the ones about records."," ","-**Your jobs, across servers.** The Jobs pages list every job on every","-server you added, side by side. You filter them by server and by","-workspace, open one, and act on it wherever it runs. These pages stay as","-they are.","+**Records, per server or across all.** Jobs, Audit Log and Costs read one","+server, or every server you added, side by side. All servers is one more","+choice in the server picker, so you filter by server the same way on each","+of these pages. You open a job, an entry or a turn and act on it wherever","+it lives."," ","-**One server at a time.** Every other page belongs to the server you pick","-at the top: Workflows, Constraints, Capabilities, Audit Log, Evals, Costs,","-Verification, Engine and Settings. A page never mixes two","-servers, because each server has its own rules and its own records.","+**Rules, one server at a time.** Workflows, Constraints, Capabilities,","+Evals, Verification, Engine and Settings belong to the server you pick. A","+rules page never mixes two servers, because each server's rules shape only","+its own jobs, and a sum of two rule sets means nothing."," "," ## What a server holds"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/VISION.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7cfdc7e1-0103-4d01-8be4-e6f52188c930","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion"