{"parentUuid":"38e6ca19-2622-4c51-a8d4-46d69d16c164","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","snippet":"26\t- The switcher lists each server with a dot for its stream, and \"All\n27\t  servers\" on a records page.\n28\t- If \"All servers\" is picked and you open a rules page, the page shows the\n29\t  last server you picked alone.\n30\t- The Jobs page follows the switcher, and its own server filter goes.\n31\t- Exit, live: switch between `local` and all servers on Jobs, and open a\n32\t  rules page from \"All servers\".\n33\t\n34\tDone 2026-11-11. The bar holds the castle, the ten pages with the count of\n35\tjobs that wait, and the switcher as one button per server. Live: Jobs\n36\tswitched from all servers to `local` and back, and Workflows opened from\n37\t\"All servers\" showed `local` alone.\n38\t\n39\t### U2. Records across servers\n40\t\n41\t- Audit Log and Costs read every server when \"All servers\" is picked.\n42\t- Each entry, turn and tally names its server. Costs add up by workspace,\n43\t  step and day across servers.\n44\t- A server that does not answer is named, and the rest still show.\n45\t- Exit, live: Costs and Audit Log show `local` and a second server\n46\t  together."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8e973f7f-6cd2-46df-acf9-63bb7bf13c04","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:58:45.836Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n26\t- The switcher lists each server with a dot for its stream, and \"All\n27\t  servers\" on a records page.\n28\t- If \"All servers\" is picked and you open a rules page, the page shows the\n29\t  last server you picked alone.\n30\t- The Jobs page follows the switcher, and its own server filter goes.\n31\t- Exit, live: switch between `local` and all servers on Jobs, and open a\n32\t  rules page from \"All servers\".\n33\t\n34\tDone 2026-11-11. The bar holds the castle, the ten pages with the count of\n35\tjobs that wait, and the switcher as one button per server. Live: Jobs\n36\tswitched from all servers to `local` and back, and Workflows opened from\n37\t\"All servers\" showed `local` alone.\n38\t\n39\t### U2. Records across servers\n40\t\n41\t- Audit Log and Costs read every server when \"All servers\" is picked.\n42\t- Each entry, turn and tally names its server. Costs add up by workspace,\n43\t  step and day across servers.\n44\t- A server that does not answer is named, and the rest still show.\n45\t- Exit, live: Costs and Audit Log show `local` and a second server\n46\t  together.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
